window.HIA=[{"slug": "iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom", "title": "IRIV EdgeAI Workshop with DRB-HICOM", "date": "13 Aug 2026", "author": "Khairul Tajudin", "topic": "training", "kind": "Workshop", "desc": "DRB-HICOM Port Klang joined a two-day IRIV EdgeAI Workshop to explore custom AI model training, logo detection and the potential of Edge AI for industrial product defect detection.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/iriv-edge-ai-workshop-with-drb-hicom-port-klang-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/iriv-edge-ai-workshop-with-drb-hicom-port-klang.png", "tags": ["IRIV EdgeAI", "DRB-HICOM", "Edge AI", "AI Vision", "Defect Detection", "Quality Inspection"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV EdgeAI Industry 4.0 Training: Getting Started with EdgeAI Vision", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/iriv-edge-ai-training-page", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-KIT-IRIV-EAI/edge-ai-kit-a-268x268.png", "price": "RM5,000.00", "old": null}], "words": 907, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>On <strong>11–12 June 2026</strong>, Cytron conducted a two-day <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/iriv-edge-ai-training-page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI Workshop</a> with three participants from <strong>DRB-HICOM Port Klang</strong>.</p><p>The workshop focused on practical Edge AI Vision development, giving participants hands-on experience with the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI</a> training platform, camera input and custom AI model training.</p><p>One of the main activities was training an AI model to <strong>detect a logo on a shirt</strong>. Instead of only demonstrating a pre-trained AI application, participants experienced how a custom detection model can be prepared, trained and tested using their own target object.</p><p>This exercise also connected directly with DRB-HICOM's intended application: exploring <strong>IRIV EdgeAI for product defect detection</strong> and automated visual inspection.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/6249276552575128225.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Objectives</h2><p>The workshop aimed to introduce participants to the complete AI Vision workflow, from preparing image data and training a model to running AI inference on an Edge AI controller.</p><p>The training also gave the DRB-HICOM team an opportunity to evaluate how the same approach could later be adapted from a simple logo-detection exercise into more practical quality-inspection applications for their own products.</p><h2>Hands-On with IRIV EdgeAI</h2><p>Throughout the workshop, participants worked directly with the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/iriv-edge-ai-training-page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI Industry 4.0 Training Kit</a>, laptops and camera systems.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/6249276552575128223.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI</a>&nbsp;training platform is based on Raspberry Pi Compute Module 5 and includes a Hailo AI accelerator for running AI workloads locally at the edge. The workshop kit also includes a USB camera and industrial components for hands-on AI and automation exercises.</p><p>Participants were introduced to areas including:</p><ul><li><p>Getting started with <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI</a></p></li><li><p>Node-RED visual programming</p></li><li><p>Camera setup for AI Vision</p></li><li><p>Custom AI dataset preparation</p></li><li><p>AI model training</p></li><li><p>Hailo AI inference using images and video</p></li><li><p>Running a custom-trained AI model</p></li><li><p>Connecting AI results with physical outputs</p></li></ul><p>The official <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/iriv-edge-ai-training-page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI Workshop</a> is designed around this combination of custom model training, camera-based inference and industrial integration, allowing participants to move beyond basic AI demonstrations into their own applications.</p><h2>Training AI to Detect a Logo</h2><p>A key hands-on exercise during the workshop was <strong>custom logo detection</strong>.</p><p>Participants used a shirt with a visible logo as the target object for the AI Vision exercise. Images were captured and used as part of the process of preparing a custom dataset and training the AI model.</p><p>Once the model was ready, a camera connected to the system was used to test the detection in a live environment.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/6249276552575128219.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>This exercise helped demonstrate an important concept in industrial AI Vision: an AI system does not have to be limited to generic objects. A model can be trained around specific visual features that are relevant to the intended application.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/iriv-edge-ai-training-page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI Workshop</a> specifically includes custom dataset preparation and inference using custom-trained models as part of its training structure.</p><h2>From Logo Detection to Product Defect Detection</h2><p>While logo detection was used as the workshop exercise, the larger objective for DRB-HICOM was to explore how the same AI Vision approach could be applied to <strong>product defect detection</strong>.</p><p>In a real inspection application, the target could change from identifying a logo to detecting visual conditions such as a missing component, incorrect assembly, surface abnormality or other product characteristics defined by the inspection requirement.</p><p>The overall development process remains similar:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/flow-edgeai-workshop.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>This is where Edge AI becomes particularly relevant for industrial quality inspection. Instead of sending every image to an external cloud system, AI inference can be performed directly at the edge, close to the camera and production process.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/6249276552575128220.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Cytron positions the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI</a> training platform for applications including defect detection, product recognition, object identification and quality inspection.</p><h2>Moving from AI Concept to Industrial Application</h2><p>For companies exploring AI Vision, one of the challenges is moving from a successful AI demonstration to something that can eventually become part of an industrial workflow.</p><p>The workshop gave participants exposure to both sides of that process.</p><p>On the AI side, they worked with image data, custom models and camera inference. On the industrial side, they explored <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI</a> as a controller that can connect AI results with other system functions.</p><p>This makes it possible to expand a vision application beyond simply displaying a detection result. Depending on the final project, an AI result could later be connected to alarms, indicators, dashboards, data recording or other automation processes.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI</a> training platform supports this combination of AI Vision and industrial integration through its camera interfaces, Node-RED environment and industrial training hardware.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-edgeai-workshop-drb-hicom/6249276552575128222.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Workshop Outcome</h2><p>By the end of the two-day workshop, the participants had experienced the basic workflow of developing a <strong>custom AI Vision application</strong>, from working with the training kit and camera to preparing and testing a trained model.</p><p>More importantly, the logo-detection exercise gave the team a practical reference for evaluating how <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI</a> could be adapted to their own product-inspection requirements.</p><p>Rather than treating AI as a standalone technology, the workshop demonstrated how AI Vision can become part of a larger industrial system for inspection, monitoring and automation.</p><p>For DRB-HICOM, the next opportunity is to apply the same workflow to actual product images and clearly defined defect conditions, moving from a training exercise towards a practical proof of concept.</p><h2>Community &amp; Next Steps</h2><p>Companies, engineers and system integrators interested in exploring <strong>AI Vision, defect detection or automated quality inspection</strong> can learn more through Cytron's <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/iriv-edge-ai-training-page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV EdgeAI Industry 4.0 Training</a> programme.</p><p>The workshop provides hands-on exposure to custom AI model training, camera-based inference and industrial Edge AI implementation.</p><p><strong>IRIV EdgeAI Industry 4.0 Training</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/iriv-edge-ai-training-page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/iriv-edge-ai-training-page</a></p><p><strong>Cytron Workshop Landing Page</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop</a></p>"}, {"slug": "iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated", "title": "IRIV PiControl Workshop with VA Integrated Corporate Sdn Bhd", "date": "07 Aug 2026", "author": "Khairul Tajudin", "topic": "training", "kind": "Workshop", "desc": "VA Integrated joined a two-day IRIV PiControl workshop at Cytron HQ to explore Node-RED, industrial control and Industry 4.0 solutions for future customer projects.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated/iriv-picontrol-workshop-with-va-integrated-corporate-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated/iriv-picontrol-workshop-with-va-integrated-corporate.png", "tags": ["IRIV PiControl", "VA Integrated", "Industry 4.0", "Node-RED", "Industrial Automation", "Digitalisation"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Workshop and Training Bundles", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-KIT-IRIV/iriv-training-kit-new-main-268x268.png", "price": "RM2,880.15++", "old": null}], "words": 475, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>On <strong>4–5 June 2026</strong>, Cytron conducted a two-day <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Workshop</a> with <strong>VA Integrated Corporate Sdn Bhd</strong> at <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cytron Headquarters</a>.</p><p>As a solution provider helping companies digitalise their operations, VA Integrated explored how <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> can support the development of Industry 4.0 solutions for its customers.</p><p>The workshop combined industrial hardware with Node-RED visual programming, allowing participants to experience how control logic, physical input and output, and browser-based dashboards can work together in one system.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated/6249276552575128217.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Hands-On with IRIV PiControl</h2><p>Throughout the workshop, participants worked directly with the<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Training Kit.</a></p><p>They connected the industrial training panels to their laptops, inspected the hardware setup and explored how the Raspberry Pi-powered controller communicates with industrial components.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated/6249276552575128214.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The workshop covered areas including:</p><ul><li><p>Getting started with IRIV PiControl</p></li><li><p>Node-RED visual programming</p></li><li><p>Industrial input and output control</p></li><li><p>Relay and push-button testing</p></li><li><p>Browser-based dashboards</p></li><li><p>Hardware and software integration</p></li><li><p>Basic system testing and troubleshooting</p></li></ul><p>This hands-on approach allowed participants to understand the complete workflow rather than learning the hardware and software separately.</p><h2>Developing Control Logic with Node-RED</h2><p>Node-RED was one of the main tools used throughout the training.</p><p>Participants built visual programming flows and connected them to the physical components inside the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> panel. They could then test how commands from the software affected the industrial hardware.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated/6249276552575128212.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The workshop demonstrated a simple connected workflow:</p><p><strong>Node-RED flow → IRIV PiControl → Industrial input and output → Dashboard and physical response</strong></p><p>Because Node-RED uses a visual flow-based interface, participants could develop, test and modify their control logic more quickly.</p><h2>Supporting Customer Digitalisation Projects</h2><p>For a solution provider, understanding both software and industrial hardware is important when developing a complete customer solution.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated/6249276552575128209.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> provides a platform for connecting sensors, machines, control components and dashboards using an industrial Raspberry Pi system.</p><p>Depending on the customer’s requirements, the platform can support solutions involving:</p><ul><li><p>Machine and equipment monitoring</p></li><li><p>Data collection and visualisation</p></li><li><p>Industrial automation</p></li><li><p>Alert and notification systems</p></li><li><p>Remote monitoring dashboards</p></li><li><p>Industrial IoT applications</p></li></ul><p>The workshop gave VA Integrated practical exposure to how these elements can be combined when developing future Industry 4.0 projects.</p><h2>Workshop Outcome</h2><p>By the end of the workshop, participants had gained practical experience with <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a>, Node-RED, industrial input and output, and dashboard development.</p><p>The training provided a foundation for VA Integrated to further explore how the platform can be adapted for its own customer requirements and Industry 4.0 solutions.</p><p>More than learning how to operate a controller, the workshop focused on understanding how hardware, software and data can be integrated into a complete digitalisation project.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-va-integrated/6249276552575128202.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Companies and solution providers interested in developing industrial automation, monitoring or digitalisation projects can explore Cytron’s <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> workshops.</p><p>The training can be adapted according to the participants’ experience, business requirements and intended industrial applications.</p><p><strong>Cytron Workshop Landing Page</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop</a></p><p><strong>IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Kit and Workshop</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops</a></p>"}, {"slug": "iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara", "title": "IRIV PiControl for WorldSkills at TVET MARA Sungai Petani", "date": "31 Jul 2026", "author": "Khairul Tajudin", "topic": "training", "kind": "Workshop", "desc": "TVET MARA Sungai Petani explored IRIV PiControl and Node-RED as a practical platform for preparing innovation projects for WorldSkills.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara/iriv-picontrol-workshop-at-tvet-mara-sungai-petani-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara/iriv-picontrol-workshop-at-tvet-mara-sungai-petani.png", "tags": ["IRIV PiControl", "TVET MARA", "Sungai Petani", "WorldSkills", "Node-RED", "Industry 4.0"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Workshop and Training Bundles", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-KIT-IRIV/iriv-training-kit-new-main-268x268.png", "price": "RM2,880.15++", "old": null}], "words": 471, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>On <strong>18–19 May 2026</strong>, Cytron conducted a two-day <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Workshop</a> at <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TVETMARASungaiPetani/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TVET MARA Sungai Petani</a>.</p><p>The workshop focused on using <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> and Node-RED to support the institution’s preparation for the <strong>WorldSkills Innovation category</strong>. Participants worked directly with industrial training panels, laptops and browser-based control interfaces to understand how software logic can interact with physical hardware.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara/6249276552575128187.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Hands-On with IRIV PiControl</h2><p>During the workshop, participants connected their laptops to the IRIV PiControl training panels and tested the system through guided hands-on activities.</p><p>They explored the industrial panel components, physical push buttons, input and output connections, and browser-based interfaces. This allowed them to observe how commands created in the software could control and monitor the connected hardware.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara/6249276552575128189.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The activities introduced participants to:</p><ul><li>IRIV PiControl and Raspberry Pi CM4</li><li>Node-RED visual programming</li><li>GPIO and relay control</li><li>Browser-based control interfaces</li><li>Industrial hardware integration</li><li>Basic system testing and troubleshooting</li></ul><h2>Building Control Logic with Node-RED</h2><p>Node-RED was one of the main tools used during the workshop.</p><p>Participants developed visual programming flows by connecting functional nodes on their laptops. These flows were then linked to the IRIV PiControl panel to control physical components such as push buttons and relays.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara/6249276552575128192.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The visual programming approach makes it easier to understand the relationship between:</p><p><strong>Node-RED flow → IRIV PiControl → Industrial input and output → Physical response</strong></p><p>This gives participants a faster way to test ideas and improve their system logic without developing every function from the beginning.</p><h2>Preparing for WorldSkills Innovation</h2><p>For the WorldSkills Innovation category, participants need more than a project idea. They must also demonstrate how the proposed system works and how it can address a practical problem.</p><p>IRIV PiControl provides a suitable platform for this preparation because it combines industrial hardware with the flexibility of Raspberry Pi and Node-RED.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara/6249276552575128184.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The platform can support prototype ideas involving automation, equipment monitoring, safety alerts, environmental data, dashboards and connected industrial systems.</p><p>During the workshop, participants experienced a basic project-development process:</p><p><strong>Develop the logic → Connect the hardware → Build the interface → Test the system → Improve the prototype</strong></p><h2>Workshop Outcome</h2><p>By the end of the workshop, participants had gained practical exposure to Node-RED, industrial input and output control, browser-based interfaces and IRIV PiControl hardware.</p><p>The workshop provided TVET MARA Sungai Petani with a foundation for continuing its WorldSkills Innovation preparation using an industrial Raspberry Pi platform.</p><p>The goal was not only to complete the workshop exercises, but also to help the team understand how IRIV PiControl can be adapted for future competition prototypes and technical training.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-worldskills-tvet-mara/6249276552575128183.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Training institutions and competition teams interested in developing industrial automation or innovation projects can explore Cytron’s IRIV PiControl workshops.</p><p>The training can be adapted according to the participants’ experience, project requirements and competition objectives.</p><p><strong>Cytron Workshop Landing Page</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop</a></p><p><strong>IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Kit and Workshop</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops</a></p>"}, {"slug": "iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship-campus", "title": "IRIV PiControl Workshop at Peninsula College, The Ship Campus", "date": "24 Jul 2026", "author": "Khairul Tajudin", "topic": "training", "kind": "Workshop", "desc": "Cytron conducted a two-day IRIV PiControl Workshop at Peninsula College, The Ship Campus, involving 10 lecturers from Computer, Electronics and Mathematics faculties.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/iriv-picontrol-workshop-at-peninsula-college-the-ship-campus-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/iriv-picontrol-workshop-at-peninsula-college-the-ship-campus.png", "tags": ["IRIV PiControl", "Peninsula College", "The Ship Campus", "Industry 4.0", "Industrial Automation", "Industrial IoT"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Workshop and Training Bundles", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-KIT-IRIV/iriv-training-kit-new-main-268x268.png", "price": "RM2,880.15++", "old": null}], "words": 873, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>On <strong>5–6 May</strong>, Cytron conducted a two-day <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Workshop</a>&nbsp;at <a href=\"https://peninsulacollege.edu.my/the-ship-campus/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Peninsula&nbsp;College, The Ship Campus, Batu Kawan</a>, with the participation of <strong>10 lecturers</strong> from the faculties of <strong>Computer, Electronics and Mathematics</strong>.</p><p>Held at one of the most distinctive modern private college campuses in Malaysia, the workshop was more than a technical training session. It was also a meaningful step towards introducing <strong>industrial-grade Raspberry Pi technology</strong> into a broader academic environment.</p><p>One of the key highlights of this workshop was Peninsula College’s interest in exploring how <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a><strong>&nbsp;can support teaching and syllabus development</strong>. This opens up opportunities for students to learn more than just theory and gain exposure to practical Industry 4.0 technologies used in real industrial environments.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/photo-6332263309373018187-w.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Objectives</h2><p>The workshop aimed to provide lecturers with hands-on experience&nbsp;with the<a href=\"\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Training Kit</a>&nbsp;while introducing practical concepts in industrial automation, industrial IoT, edge computing,&nbsp;and data monitoring.</p><p>At the same time, the session also showed how <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> can be relevant across multiple academic disciplines, especially for lecturers from Computer, Electronics and Mathematics backgrounds who are involved in shaping future learning content and curriculum.</p><h2>Hands-On Learning with an Industrial Controller</h2><p>Throughout the workshop, the lecturers gained practical exposure to the <a href=\"\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Training Kit</a> through guided demonstrations and hands-on activities.</p><p>Rather than learning only from slides or theoretical explanations, participants were able to work directly with the hardware, observe the industrial panel setup, connect the system and explore how the controller works together with laptops, dashboards and related industrial components.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/photo-6332367990610924412-w.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> is an industrial controller powered by <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-cm4-with-wireless-pick-ram-and-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Raspberry Pi Compute Module 4</strong></a>, designed for industrial monitoring and control applications.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/photo-6332367990610924411-w.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The workshop introduced participants to areas including:</p><ul><li>Getting started with IRIV PiControl and Raspberry Pi CM4</li><li>Node-RED programming and dashboard development</li><li>GPIO and industrial control concepts</li><li>Data monitoring and interface configuration</li><li>Industrial communication workflow</li><li>Basic understanding of connected Industry 4.0 systems</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/photo-6327966349212193106-w.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>These topics help lecturers understand how modern control systems work beyond conventional classroom examples, and how a Raspberry Pi-based industrial controller can be used in a more structured and real-world teaching environment.</p><h2>A Modern Learning Environment for Industry 4.0</h2><p>One unique aspect of this workshop was its location at <strong>The Ship Campus, Batu Kawan</strong>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/tsc-0018e-2048x1536.webp\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Known for its striking campus design and modern learning environment, Peninsula College reflects a progressive educational setting that is open to practical and industry-relevant technologies. Hosting the IRIV PiControl workshop in such an environment made the session especially meaningful, as it connected modern facilities with modern teaching tools.</p><p>As a private college that values current and future-ready learning approaches, Peninsula College’s interest in IRIV PiControl shows that Industry 4.0 learning is no longer limited to traditional engineering settings alone. It can also be introduced across broader academic pathways where digital systems, automation and applied technology are becoming increasingly important.</p><h2>Expanding Learning Across Multiple Faculties</h2><p>Another important highlight of the workshop was the diversity of the participating lecturers.</p><p>The 10 lecturers came from the faculties of <strong>Computer, Electronics and Mathematics</strong>, showing that the relevance of IRIV PiControl goes beyond a single department.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/photo-6327966349212193102-w.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>For Computer-related teaching, IRIV PiControl introduces areas such as Node-RED, system logic, interfacing and data handling. For Electronics-related subjects, it provides practical exposure to industrial hardware integration, control panels, input/output systems and industrial communication.</p><p>For Mathematics-related disciplines, it opens possibilities for applying logical thinking, data analysis and system behaviour concepts in a more practical context.</p><p>This cross-faculty interest is significant because it shows that Industry 4.0 technologies can support interdisciplinary learning, not only for engineering students but also for a wider tertiary audience.</p><h2>Demo / Results</h2><p>One of the most meaningful outcomes of the workshop was Peninsula College’s interest in using <strong>IRIV PiControl as part of teaching and syllabus exploration</strong>.</p><p>This is an encouraging direction, because it means students may eventually gain exposure to <strong>industrial-grade Raspberry Pi systems</strong> in their learning journey, instead of only focusing on conventional tools or isolated theory-based exercises.</p><p>By integrating platforms such as IRIV PiControl into academic delivery, students can better understand how industrial systems are built and connected — from control logic and hardware integration to user dashboards and monitoring.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-workshop-peninsula-college-the-ship/photo-6327966349212193103-w.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>This gives learners a stronger connection between classroom content and the kinds of technologies increasingly used in modern industrial environments.</p><h2>Preparing More Institutions for Industry 4.0</h2><p>The Peninsula College workshop demonstrates how collaboration between educational institutions and technology providers can help make technical education more relevant to current industry needs.</p><p>Cytron’s IRIV PiControl workshop is designed for lecturers, trainers, engineers, system integrators and institutions that want practical exposure to industrial automation and digitalisation.</p><p>As more colleges and universities begin to explore industrial IoT, edge computing and connected monitoring systems, platforms like IRIV PiControl can help bridge the gap between academic learning and real industrial application.</p><p>The goal is not simply to introduce another controller, but to support institutions in preparing students for the technologies, workflows and thinking required in Industry 4.0.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Institutions that are interested in introducing <strong>industrial Raspberry Pi-based control and monitoring</strong> into their teaching, training or curriculum can explore Cytron’s available workshop offerings and training kits.</p><h3>Explore the Workshop</h3><p><strong>Cytron Workshop Landing Page</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop</a></p><h3>Explore the Training Kit</h3><p><strong>IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Kit and Workshop</strong><br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/c-workshop-seminar/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops</a></p>"}, {"slug": "jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop", "title": "From Workshop to Curriculum: JMTI Explores IRIV PiControl for Industry 4.0 Education", "date": "17 Jul 2026", "author": "Khairul Tajudin", "topic": "training", "kind": "Workshop", "desc": "Ten lecturers from JMTI’s Mechatronics faculty joined a two-day IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Workshop, marking an important step towards incorporating Raspberry Pi-powered industrial control", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop/bringing-industrial-raspberry-pi-into-tvet-education-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop/bringing-industrial-raspberry-pi-into-tvet-education.png", "tags": ["IRIV PiControl", "Industry 4.0", "JMTI", "Industrial Automation", "Industrial IoT", "Raspberry Pi CM4"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Workshop and Training Bundles", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-KIT-IRIV/iriv-training-kit-new-main-268x268.png", "price": "RM2,880.15++", "old": null}], "words": 674, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>On 6–7 April 2026, Cytron conducted a two-day IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Workshop with 10 lecturers from the Mechatronics faculty at Japan-Malaysia Technical Institute, or JMTI.</p><p>More than a technical training session, the workshop marked an important step towards bringing Raspberry Pi-powered industrial control into tertiary education. One of the most meaningful outcomes of the workshop was JMTI’s interest in incorporating IRIV PiControl into its curriculum.</p><p>This would allow future students to gain hands-on experience with a locally designed industrial controller during their tertiary education—not only learning how individual technologies work, but also how they are integrated into a complete Industry 4.0 system.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop/6253653485027003808.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Objectives</h2><p>The workshop aimed to give JMTI lecturers practical experience with an industrial Raspberry Pi-based controller and introduce technologies related to industrial automation, industrial IoT, edge processing, monitoring and data communication.</p><p>The workshop also provided an opportunity to explore how IRIV PiControl could be incorporated into JMTI’s curriculum, allowing students to learn modern industrial technologies alongside conventional PLC programming and Assembly Language.</p><h2>Hands-On Learning with an Industrial Controller</h2><p>Throughout the workshop, the lecturers gained practical experience using the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Training Kit</a>.</p><p>Rather than learning only through presentations, participants worked directly with industrial training panels, connected hardware, configured the system and developed applications using their own laptops.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop/6253733736490929701.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>IRIV PiControl is an industrial controller powered by Raspberry Pi Compute Module 4. The workshop kit combines it with components such as a DIN rail, industrial 24V power supply, RS485 temperature and humidity sensor, and single-phase AC power meter.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop/6253733736490929697.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The training introduced participants to areas including:</p><ul><li>Getting started with IRIV PiControl and Raspberry Pi CM4</li><li>Node-RED programming and dashboard development</li><li>RS485 sensor and power meter integration</li><li>MQTT communication</li><li>Industrial data collection and monitoring</li><li>Basic Python and Linux operation</li></ul><p>These topics reflect the skills required to build connected Industry 4.0 systems, from collecting machine data to displaying information on a dashboard and communicating with other industrial devices.</p><h2>Expanding Industrial Education Beyond Conventional Control</h2><p>PLC programming and Assembly Language remain important foundations in industrial and embedded-system education. However, modern engineers are increasingly expected to understand additional technologies such as industrial IoT, Linux, Python, databases, dashboards and edge computing.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop/6253733736490929696.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>IRIV PiControl helps connect these areas in one platform. Students can learn how a Raspberry Pi-based system operates within an industrial environment while gaining exposure to real industrial interfaces, sensors and communication protocols.</p><p>This complements conventional automation subjects and prepares them to work with both operational technology and modern software-based systems.</p><h2>Results</h2><p>One of the most meaningful outcomes of the workshop was JMTI’s interest in incorporating IRIV PiControl into its curriculum. By introducing IRIV PiControl into the syllabus, students could explore the full journey of industrial data:</p><p><strong>Sensor and machine data → Industrial communication → Edge processing → Dashboard and database → Monitoring and automation</strong></p><p>This provides a practical bridge between classroom knowledge and the systems students may encounter in modern factories, automation projects and system-integration environments.</p><p>The goal is not simply to teach another controller. It is to give students the opportunity to understand how modern industrial systems communicate, process information and make decisions.</p><h2>Preparing More Institutions for Industry 4.0</h2><p>The JMTI workshop demonstrates how collaboration between educational institutions and technology providers can help keep technical education aligned with current industry needs.</p><p>Cytron’s IRIV PiControl workshop is designed for lecturers, trainers, engineers, system integrators and researchers who want practical exposure to industrial automation and digitalisation.</p><p>Custom and on-site training can also be arranged to suit an institution’s technical requirements and learning objectives.</p><p>As more institutions introduce industrial IoT, edge computing and data-driven automation into their programmes, students can graduate with broader and more relevant technical experience.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jmti-iriv-picontrol-industry-4-workshop/6253653485027003805.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Universities, polytechnics and TVET institutions interested in incorporating Raspberry Pi-powered industrial control into their syllabus can explore the IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Workshop or discuss a customised training programme with Cytron’s training team.</p><h3>Explore the Workshop</h3><p>Learn more about Cytron’s available training programmes: <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/cytron-workshop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cytron Workshop</a></p><h3>Explore the Training Kit</h3><p>Learn more about the hardware, training kit and workshop programme:<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-industry-4p0-kit-and-workshops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl Industry 4.0 Kit and Workshop</a></p>"}, {"slug": "milesight-cytron-iot-solutions-malaysia", "title": "Cytron Partners with Milesight for IoT Solutions in Malaysia", "date": "18 Dec 2025", "author": "Iffah Nasri", "topic": "partners", "kind": "Partnership", "desc": "Cytron partners with Milesight to provide trusted IoT solutions in Malaysia, including the SIRIM-certified Milesight UG65 LoRaWAN® gateway.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/milesight-cytron-iot-solutions-malaysia/milesight--cytron-1-320x180.jpeg", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/milesight-cytron-iot-solutions-malaysia/milesight--cytron-1.jpeg", "tags": ["Milesight"], "products": [], "words": 306, "useCase": false, "body": "Cytron Technologies is pleased to announce a <strong>strategic collaboration with Milesight</strong>, a global provider of innovative IoT products, to support the deployment of reliable and compliant IoT solutions in Malaysia.<br> &nbsp;Through this partnership, <strong>Cytron acts as a trusted local reseller and support partner</strong>, offering Milesight’s portfolio of <strong>LoRaWAN® sensors, gateways, controllers, and routers</strong> to the Malaysian market. This collaboration enables individuals, solution providers, and businesses to access globally recognised IoT technology with <strong>local availability, support, and deployment readiness</strong>.<hr><h2>Supporting Deployment Readiness and Local Compliance</h2>As part of this collaboration, Cytron is also pleased to share that the <strong>Milesight UG65 Semi-Industrial LoRaWAN® Gateway</strong> offered by Cytron has officially obtained the <strong>SIRIM Certificate of Conformity (CoC)</strong>.<br> &nbsp;This certification confirms that the UG65 meets Malaysia’s local safety and technical requirements, supporting <strong>compliant IoT deployments</strong> in enterprise, industrial, and infrastructure environments. With SIRIM approval, customers can deploy the gateway with greater confidence for local projects.<hr><h2>Reliable IoT Solutions with Local Support</h2>The Milesight UG65 is designed for <strong>smart building and industrial applications</strong>, where stable performance and long-term reliability are important. Together with Cytron’s local technical support and distribution capabilities, this helps reduce deployment risk and supports smoother project implementation.<br> &nbsp;By combining <strong>Milesight’s global IoT technology</strong> with <strong>Cytron’s local expertise</strong>, the partnership aims to better support Malaysia’s growing demand for practical, scalable IoT solutions.<hr><h2>Expanding a Trusted and Certified IoT Ecosystem</h2>Cytron is currently working with Milesight to obtain <strong>SIRIM CoC for additional LoRaWAN® gateways and sensor nodes</strong>. This ongoing effort reflects Cytron’s commitment to building a <strong>trusted and compliant IoT ecosystem</strong> for the Malaysian market.<br> &nbsp;Further updates will be shared as more products achieve certification.<p>To learn more about the <strong>Milesight UG65 Semi-Industrial LoRaWAN® Gateway</strong>, visit:<br> <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-ug65-semi-industrial-lorawan-gateway-with-without-cellular\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/p-ug65-semi-industrial-lorawan-gateway-with-without-cellular</a></p><p>For enquiries on Milesight IoT solutions in Malaysia, feel free to contact the Cytron team.</p>"}, {"slug": "success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol", "title": "Success Story: Smart Factory Power Monitoring with IRIV PiControl", "date": "10 Dec 2025", "author": "Raden Fatih", "topic": "projects", "kind": "Customer project", "desc": "ESG stands for Environmental, Social and Governance. It is a way to measure how responsible and sustainable an organization is:", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/smart-factory-power-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/smart-factory-power-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol.png", "tags": ["IRIV PiControl", "Power Meter Data Monitoring", "Raspberry Pi in Industry", "IRIV Pi Control"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Acrel ADL Power Meter (RS485 Modbus/RTU)", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-adl-power-meter", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-ADL-PMETER/v-adl-pmeter-main-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM149.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Meanwell Industry DIN Rail Mount Power Supply 24V", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-meanwell-industry-din-rail-mount-power-supply-24v", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-PS-MDR-24V/main-photo-268x268.png", "price": "RM98.00++", "old": null}], "words": 642, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>What is ESG?</h2><p>ESG stands for Environmental, Social and Governance. It is a way to measure how responsible and sustainable an organization is:</p><ul><li>E - Environmental: How effeciently energy and resources are used, carbon footprint and waste reduction.</li><li>S - Social: Employee welfare, safety, community impact.</li><li>G - Governance: Transparency, compliance, ethical operations.</li></ul><p>For the Environmental (E) part, accurate energy data is a key requirement. Without a real power consumption data, it is difficult to prove real environmental performance. That is where this power monitoring system direcly supports ESG.</p><h2><br> Problem Statement</h2><p><br> Energy efficiency is no longer a luxury, it is a necessity. With rising electricity costs and growing ESG (Environmental, Social &amp; Governance) awareness, having clear visibility of power consumption is the first step towards smarter and more effective and sustainable operations.</p><h2>Solution</h2><p>By using power meter with <strong>IRIV PiControl</strong> together, you gain the ability to monitor real-time electrical readings such as voltage, current, power, energy usage, power factor, and frequency. The IRIV PiControl acts as central hub<strong>,</strong>it collects data from the power meter via RS485 Modbus, processes it efficiently, and sends it to your database. All readings are then displayed on a clean and sleek Grafana web dashboard, with data stored securely in MySQL&nbsp;for accurate long-term tracking and analysis.</p><h2>Hardware Setup</h2><p>List of Hardware:<br> </p><p>1. IRIV PiControl</p><p>2. Acrel ADL400 three-phase power meter</p><p>3. Meanwell Industry DIN Rail Mount Power Supply 24V</p><p>4. Circuit Breaker</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/photo-6181327846375099799-y.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 1: Acrel ADL400 three-phase power meter installed in the electrical panel</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/photo-6181327846375099800-y.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 2: RS485 Modbus Connection from Acrel ADL400 to IRIV PiControl</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/ct-clamp.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 3: CT clamps attached to each phase for current measurement</p><p>The power meter&nbsp;reads electrical data through CT clamps and sends it to IRIV PiControl via RS485 Modbus. The setup is compact, reliable, and suitable for industrial, lab, or SME environments.</p><h2>From Meter to Dashboard In Real-Time</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/screenshot-2025-12-10-173612.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 4: Node-RED flow reading Modbus data from the ADL400 power meter</p><p>Power data is processed using Node-RED, stored in MySQL and visualized in Grafana. With Cloudflared remote access, you can securely monitor energy usage from anywhere.</p><h2>Secure Data Logging</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/screenshot-2025-12-10-180317.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 5: Historical voltage, current and power data stored in MySQL</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/screenshot-2025-12-10-180334.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 6: Total Energy data stored for respective day</p><p>All readings are stored for daily, weekly and long-term analysis which is perfect for performance tracking and ESG Documentation.</p><h2>Real-Time Dashboard</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/95.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 7: Real-time three phase power monitoring on Grafana</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/screenshot-2025-12-10-174319.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Figure 8: Real-time three phase monitoring on Node-RED</p><p>Clear visual dashboards turn raw electrical data into easy-to-understand insights for technical an non-technical users alike.</p><h2>Why this Matters for ESG &amp; Sustainability</h2><p>Real-time power monitoring helps:</p><ul><li>Detect energy wastage</li><li>Optimise electricity usage</li><li>Reduce operating costs</li><li>Lower carbon footprint</li><li>Support ESG and sustainability reporting</li></ul><p>Data makes sustainability measurable, not just a promise.</p><h2>Who is this for?</h2><ul><li>Factories and industrial users</li><li>SMEs and workshops</li><li>Universities and R&amp;D labs</li><li>ESG-focused organizations</li><li>Makers and IoT Developers</li></ul><h2>Start Building Today</h2><p>Follow our step-by-step tutorials to build your own real-time monitoring system:</p><p><br> 1.<a href=\"design-h-tutorial.html?slug=iriv-mysql-grafana-cloudflared-public\">IRIV PiControl - MySQL to Grafana Data Remote Access</a></p><p>2.<a href=\"design-h-tutorial.html?slug=irivpicontrol-adl400-powermeter-mysql-dashboardmonitor\">&nbsp;IRIV PiControl - 3 Phase Power Meter Data Monitoring PART-1</a></p><p>3.<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/tutorial/irivpicontrol-adl400-powermeter-mysql-dashboardmonitor2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl - 3 Phase Power Meter Data Monitoring PART-2</a></p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>The solution is more than just monitoring, it is a practical step towards smarter energy management, helping organizations track and optimize their energy usage in real time. Beyond operational effiency, it supports ESG compliance by providing transparent data for sustainability reporting, reduces operational costs through informed energy decisions and ultimately contributes to a greener more sustainable future. By integrating technology with environmental rensponsibility, this approach empowers businesss to make smarter choices that benefit both their bottom line and the planet.</p><h2>Summary</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-factory-monitoring-with-iriv-p/iriv-application-infographic.webp\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a>&nbsp;has shown the performance and endurance of Industrial edge controllers. The openness of its architecture, ready with Raspberry Pi OS, and support from many software makes it the perfect choice for this project.</p>"}, {"slug": "maistorage-aidaptiv-llm-training", "title": "Empowering Our Team Through Edge AI Innovation: Highlights from the MaiStorage aiDAPTIV+ Training", "date": "08 Dec 2025", "author": "Rupa", "topic": "training", "kind": "Training", "desc": "Our team explores aiDAPTIV+, MaiStorage’s edge AI solution for secure, cost-effective on-premises LLM training and high-performance inference.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/maistorage-aidaptiv-llm-training/thumbnail-nvidia-ai-17-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/maistorage-aidaptiv-llm-training/thumbnail-nvidia-ai-17.png", "tags": ["aiDAPTIV+", "MaiStorage", "Edge AI", "LLM Training", "NVIDIA AI", "Seminars & Workshop"], "products": [], "words": 606, "useCase": false, "body": "<h1>Introduction:</h1><p>Our team recently attended a focused two-day workshop in Puchong hosted by <strong>MaiStorage</strong>, a member of the <strong>Phison Group</strong>, where we explored their latest breakthrough: <strong>aiDAPTIV+</strong>, a complete solution designed to make large model training and inference practical, affordable, and deployable at the edge.</p><p>This workshop offered our team a hands-on understanding of how aiDAPTIV+ enables organizations to run advanced AI workloads such as fine-tuning large language models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and high-speed inference<strong>directly on-premises</strong>, keeping data secure while dramatically lowering costs.</p><h1>Understanding aiDAPTIV+: Bringing LLM Capabilities to the Edge:</h1><p>One of the core messages from the training was how aiDAPTIV+ redefines what’s possible with edge AI. Traditional LLM training relies heavily on expensive, power-hungry GPU infrastructure and high-bandwidth memory (HBM). MaiStorage's aiDAPTIV+ introduces a new model: using <strong>cost-effective flash memory</strong>, combined with Phison’s optimized middleware, to expand GPU memory and support large-scale model training at a fraction of the typical cost.</p><p>With this architecture, aiDAPTIV+ supports a wide range of training and inference scenarios from compact <strong>8B parameter models</strong> on notebooks to full <strong>405B parameter</strong> workloads on servers. This flexibility provides a path for organizations of any size to adopt and scale AI capabilities based on their budget and deployment needs.</p><h1>Key Capabilities We Explored During the Workshop:</h1><h2>1. On-Premises LLM Training with Full Data Control</h2><p>aiDAPTIV+ allows organizations to fine-tune and run LLMs entirely within their own environment. This means sensitive data never leaves the premises, ensuring privacy, security, and compliance while still gaining the benefits of advanced AI processing.</p><h2>2. GPU Memory Expansion via aiDAPTIVCache</h2><p>A standout piece of technology covered during the training was the <strong>AI100E SSD</strong>, paired with middleware that extends GPU memory by <strong>320GB on PCs</strong> and up to <strong>8TB on high-performance systems</strong>.&nbsp;This memory extension is optimized for PyTorch and works seamlessly without requiring modifications to existing AI applications, significantly reducing bottlenecks during LLM training.</p><h2>3. Scalable Architecture for Any Model Size</h2><p>Depending on deployment requirements, aiDAPTIV+ can operate on a range of hardware from edge devices (<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-nvidia-jetson-orin-nano-8gb-kits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jetson Orin Nano</a>, Jetson Orin NX, <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-nvidia-jetson-agx-orin-kits-and-bundles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jetson AGX Orin</a>)&nbsp;and desktops to workstations and servers supporting model sizes from 8B up to 405B parameters.This scalability gives teams the flexibility to start small and expand as their AI workloads grow.</p><h2>4. End-to-End AI Workflow Tools</h2><p>The training also highlighted the <strong>aiDAPTIVPro Suite</strong>, an intuitive, all-in-one software environment that covers the entire AI pipeline.&nbsp;This allows teams to manage every step of their AI workflow through a graphical interface.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/maistorage-aidaptiv-llm-training/untitled-diagram.drawio-2.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><strong>AI Pipeline Flow</strong></p><h2>5. Broad Model Support</h2><p>aiDAPTIV+ currently supports many leading models including Llama, Falcon, Vicuna,&nbsp;Whisper, Mistral, and more with new models being added continuously.</p><h1></h1><h1>Hands-On Learning: What Our Team Gained:</h1><p>Through interactive sessions, our team gained practical skills and insights, including:</p><ul><li><p>Fine-tuning LLMs using local datasets</p></li><li><p>Running inference workloads efficiently</p></li><li><p>Using the aiDAPTIVPro Suite for end-to-end experimentation</p></li></ul><p>This knowledge will directly support our ongoing efforts to adopt and deliver AI solutions that are secure, cost-effective, and operationally efficient.</p><h1>The Impact: A New Era of Accessible Edge AI:</h1><p>aiDAPTIV+ demonstrates that advanced AI no longer requires massive cloud infrastructure. By combining GPU processing with intelligently managed flash memory, Phison and MaiStorage are making it possible for businesses to run large models where data is created, minimizing cloud costs and accelerating insights. For our team, this workshop marks an important step forward. We now have a deeper understanding of edge-optimized AI workflows and how solutions like aiDAPTIV+ can support our future innovations and customer offerings.</p><p>We extend our gratitude to MaiStorage and the team of trainers for hosting this insightful and impactful training session.</p>"}, {"slug": "success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol", "title": "Success Story: Smart Compressor Room Monitoring with IRIV PiControl", "date": "04 Sep 2025", "author": "Raden Fatih", "topic": "projects", "kind": "Customer project", "desc": "Motor compressors are widely used in industrial environments and play a critical role in powering machinery. However, one of the most important challenges is monitoring their internal temperature.…", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol/smart-compressor-room-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol/smart-compressor-room-monitoring-with-iriv-picontrol.png", "tags": ["IRIV PiControl", "Raspberry Pi", "Sensor", "Raspberry Pi in Industry", "IRIV Pi Control"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "SHT40 Temperature & Humidity Sensor with RS485 Support", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-sht40-rs485-temperature-and-humidity-sensor", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-SN-HUTE-RS485/v-sn-hute-rs485-main-268x268.png", "price": "RM35.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Meanwell Industry DIN Rail Mount Power Supply 24V", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-meanwell-industry-din-rail-mount-power-supply-24v", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-PS-MDR-24V/main-photo-268x268.png", "price": "RM98.00++", "old": null}], "words": 695, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Problem Statement</h2><p>Motor compressors are widely used in industrial environments and play a critical role in powering machinery. However, one of the most important challenges is monitoring their internal temperature. Overheating can cause serious damage, leading to unexpected downtime and costly repairs.</p><p>The main issue was identifying whether temperature spikes were caused by external environmental factors (such as direct sunlight hitting the compressor) or by the compressor’s own internal operation. Without proper monitoring, it becomes difficult to prevent overheating-related failure.</p><h2>Solution</h2><p>To tackle this challenge, we designed a monitoring system using IRIV PiControl paired with three industrial-grade SHT40 temperature and humidity sensors. Each sensor was placed at a different location on the compressor to capture detailed readings.</p><p>The data is continuously collected and processed through Node-RED, which handles three key tasks:</p><ol><li><p>Logging readings into a text file for local storage.<br> </p></li><li><p>Inserting readings into a MySQL database via phpMyAdmin for long-term tracking.<br> </p></li><li><p>Displaying data on a Node-RED dashboard for real-time monitoring and historical analysis.<br> </p></li></ol><p>This setup makes it possible to clearly visualize temperature patterns and determine whether spikes come from sunlight exposure or compressor activity.</p><h2>Hardware Setup</h2><p>Components used:</p><ul><li><p>IRIV PiControl – the main controller used to acquire sensor data and run Node-RED.</p></li><li><p>3× Industrial Grade SHT40 Temperature &amp; Humidity Sensors – chosen for high accuracy and reliability in industrial conditions.</p></li></ul><p>Sensor Placement:</p><p>To capture accurate readings from different parts of the compressor, three sensors were installed in separate locations:</p><p>Sensor 1: Inside the compressor casing to capture internal heating.</p><p>Sensor 2: At the compressor blower to measure incoming air temperature.</p><p>Sensor 3: Placed at the top of the motor compressor to measure surrounding temperature.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-wit/photo-2025-09-02-16-18-29.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><em>Figure 1.1 SHT40 Sensor Placed inside the Motor Compressor's Casing</em></p><p><em><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-wit/photo-2025-09-02-16-18-28.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></p><p><em>Figure 1.2 SHT40 Sensor Placed at the Motor Compressor's Blower</em></p><p><em><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-wit/photo-2025-09-02-16-18-28-2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></p><p><em>Figure 1.3 SHT40 Sensor Placed at the top of the Motor Compressor's Casing</em></p><p><em><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-wit/photo-2025-09-02-16-18-29-2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></p><p><em>Figure 1.4 IRIV PiControl installed with DIN Rail at the side of the Motor Compressor</em></p><h2>Project Concept</h2><p>The sensors continuously feed data into the PiControl. Node-RED collects the readings at fixed time intervals and performs three key tasks:</p><ol><li><p>Save the readings into a text file for local reference. <a href=\"design-h-tutorial.html?slug=iriv-picontrol-write-sensor-readings-into-a-text-file\">(IRIV PiControl - Write Sensor Readings into a Text File)</a><br> </p></li><li><p>Insert the readings into a MySQL database through phpMyAdmin for long-term storage.<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/tutorial/iriv-logging-data-to-mysql-with-node-red\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">(IRIV PiControl - Logging Data to MySQL With Node-RED)</a><br> </p></li><li><p>Display the readings on a Node-RED dashboard with both real-time and historical charts.<a href=\"design-h-tutorial.html?slug=iriv-picontrol-time-series-line-chart-with-mysql\">(IRIV PiControl - Time-Series Line Chart with MySQL)</a></p></li></ol><h2>Software Implementation</h2><h3>Node-RED</h3><p>Node-RED serves as the central programming environment. The following nodes are used:</p><ul><li><p>Write File Node – writes readings into a text file.<br> </p></li><li><p>MySQL Node – sends data to phpMyAdmin.<br> </p></li><li><p>Date Picker Node – selects date and time range for historical analysis.<br> </p></li><li><p>Function Node – processes readings and formats queries.<br> </p></li><li><p>Chart Node – visualizes data in real time and as a time series line chart.</p></li></ul><h3>phpMyAdmin MySQL Database</h3><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-wit/image5.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><em>Figure 1.5 MySQL Database</em></p><p>The database is structured as follows:</p><ul><li><p>Table Name: Motor_Compressor,Blower,Environment<br> </p></li><li><p>Columns:</p><ul><li><p>temperature</p></li><li><p>time<br> </p></li></ul></li></ul><p>This setup allows efficient storage and retrieval of historical data, which can be accessed directly from Node-RED.</p><h2>Dashboard Visualization</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/success-story-smart-compressor-room-monitoring-wit/image1.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><em>Figure 1.6 Finished Dashboard</em></p><p>The Node-RED dashboard provides:</p><ul><li><p>Real-time readings from all three sensors (displayed as gauges).<br> </p></li><li><p>Historical analysis using the date picker and time series chart.<br> </p></li><li><p>Clear comparison of temperature fluctuations over time.</p></li></ul><h2><meta><b>Conclusion</b></h2><p>This project demonstrated that IRIV PiControl with three SHT40 sensors can effectively monitor motor compressor temperature. Using Node-RED and phpMyAdmin MySQL, we achieved both real-time monitoring and historical data visualization.</p><p>The system helps identify whether temperature spikes are caused by environmental conditions or by the compressor’s operation. This contributes to better predictive maintenance, reduced downtime, and extended equipment life.</p><p><strong>Brief introduction of IRIV PiControl:</strong><br> The IRIV PiControl is an industrial-grade controller designed for data acquisition, monitoring, and control applications. Powered by a Raspberry Pi Compute Module, it features multiple I/O ports, supports industrial protocols like Modbus and OPC UA, and enables integration with cloud platforms via MQTT. It's ideal for Industrial IoT (IIoT), automation, and smart factory solutions.</p><p>For more information about the IRIV PiControl, please visit<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol</a></p><p>If you have a use case you’d like to share with us, feel free to email us at:<a>myindustry@cytron.io</a>.</p>"}, {"slug": "AIHorizon25", "title": "Empowering Edge AI: Highlights from the AI Horizon Exhibition at SPICE Arena Penang", "date": "11 Aug 2025", "author": "HY Ng", "topic": "partners", "kind": "Exhibition", "desc": "Cutting-edge industrial AI demos at the AI Horizon Exhibition, where Vision & Edge AI came to life with Cytron’s IRIV EdgeAI and PiControl", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/aihorizon25/photo-9-2025-08-10-21-50-35-320x180.jpg", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/aihorizon25/photo-9-2025-08-10-21-50-35.jpg", "tags": ["IRIV EdgeAI", "Raspberry Pi for AI", "AI applications"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV EdgeAI CM5 - IR4.0 Industrial AI Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-EAI5/iriv-edgeai-cm5-view-1-1-268x268.png", "price": "RM2,487.00++", "old": null}], "words": 280, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Empowering Edge AI: Highlights from the AI Horizon Exhibition at SPICE Arena<br> Penang | 8-9 August 2025</h2><p><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/aihorizon25/photo-5-2025-08-10-21-50-35.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></strong></p><p>We had a fantastic time at the <strong>AI Horizon Exhibition</strong> at SPICE Arena, organised by Tech Dome Penang with the support of dedicated partners and stakeholders.</p><p><strong>Thousands of visitors</strong> — from students to professionals- turned up to witness AI in action.</p><p><br> Attendees enjoyed a variety of AI-driven activities, including:</p><ul><li><p>Coding competitions test the creativity and critical thinking of youth</p></li><li><p>The <em>Young Engineers</em> programme introduces schoolchildren to AI-based engineering</p></li><li><p>Industry conferences, public forums, and innovation showcases by SMEs, start-ups, and multinational firms</p></li></ul><p>We also showcased two of our latest innovations in <strong>Edge AI</strong> and <strong>Industry 4.0 solutions</strong>:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/aihorizon25/photo-1-2025-08-10-21-50-35.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h3>IRIV EdgeAI</h3><p>🔗 <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-edge-ai-cm5</a></p><p>A compact, industrial-grade AI system powered by Raspberry Pi CM5 and <strong>HAILO AI processors</strong>, built to run <strong>vision AI models</strong> directly at the edge.</p><h3>What it can do:</h3><p><br> ✅ Detect and classify objects in real time<br> ✅ Inspect products for defects<br> ✅ Count items, read labels, monitor assembly lines<br> ✅ Trigger automation from visual cues</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/aihorizon25/photo-3-2025-08-10-21-50-35.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h3>IRIV PiControl</h3><p>An industrial Raspberry Pi-based controller for <strong>data collection and automation</strong>.</p><ul><li><p>Collects data from sensors, PLCs, and machines</p></li><li><p>Controls equipment based on AI or sensor inputs</p></li><li><p>Supports Industry 4.0 protocols like Serial and Modbus</p></li></ul><p><strong>Together</strong>, IRIV EdgeAI + PiControl form a <strong>complete Industry 4.0 solution</strong> — from defect detection to automated process control.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/aihorizon25/photo-2025-08-13-15-09-46-2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><hr><p>A big thank you to everyone who visited our booth and exchanged ideas with us. Your engagement fuels our mission to make industrial AI more accessible, scalable, and future-proof.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/aihorizon25/photo-11-2025-08-10-21-50-35.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>📩 <strong>Interested in Vision &amp; Edge AI for your operations?</strong><br> Reach out and start the conversation. Reach me at hyng@cytron.io!</p>&nbsp;"}, {"slug": "ai-workshop-ciast-raspberry-pi-esp32-tvet", "title": "Empowering TVET: AI Workshop with Raspberry Pi & ESP32", "date": "07 Aug 2025", "author": "Iffah Nasri", "topic": "training", "kind": "Workshop", "desc": "Cytron and CIAST empower TVET educators with hands-on AI training using Raspberry Pi 5 and ESP32. Real-time vision and motion AI made easy for classrooms.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/ai-workshop-ciast-raspberry-pi-esp32-tvet/ciast-cytron-ai-1-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/ai-workshop-ciast-raspberry-pi-esp32-tvet/ciast-cytron-ai-1.png", "tags": [], "products": [{"name": "Raspberry Pi 5 Single Board Computer", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-5", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-RASPBERRY-PI-5/v-raspberry-pi-5-main-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM202.00++", "old": null}], "words": 528, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Empowering TVET with Edge AI: A Hands-On Journey with CIAST &amp; Cytron</h2><p><strong>Shah Alam, Selangor</strong></p><p><strong>6–7 August 2025</strong></p><p>Just recently, something exciting happened at CIAST. Together with our friends at the <strong>Centre for Instructor and Advanced Skill Training (CIAST)</strong>, we hosted a 2-day hands-on workshop diving deep into <strong>AI applications using the Raspberry Pi 5 AI Kit and ESP32</strong>. This wasn’t just another tech talk. It was a real, down-to-earth experience to show how <strong>AI can be practical, local, and affordable,</strong>&nbsp;especially for the TVET (Technical and Vocational Education and Training) community.</p><p>\"AI isn’t just for PhDs or big tech. It’s for classrooms, labs and anyone with a Raspberry Pi or ESP32.\"</p><p>The agenda was packed with real-time demos, tinkering sessions, and lots of “Aha!” moments. Here’s what we explored:</p><ul><li><p><strong>People detection &amp; object recognition</strong> using Raspberry Pi 5 + Hailo-8 AI HAT+</p></li><li><p><strong>Gesture recognition</strong> on ESP32 powered by Edge Impulse</p></li><li><p>&nbsp;Hands-on: model training, deployment, debugging, and problem-solving</p></li></ul><p>It wasn’t long before participants got excited, especially when their own boards started detecting motion or blinking LEDs in response to a trained gesture.</p><p>“I didn’t think this was possible without a cloud connection or GPU!”</p><p>That’s something we heard more than once, and it never gets old.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/ai-workshop-ciast-raspberry-pi-esp32-tvet/photo-6-2025-08-07-09-39-49.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h3>This collaboration meant a lot to us.</h3><p>CIAST approached us with a simple yet powerful goal: help instructors bring AI into the classroom in a way that makes sense not just theory, but tools their students can actually build with.</p><p>And that aligns perfectly with what we believe in.</p><p>\"If we want AI to be inclusive, we have to make it reachable, not intimidating. That starts with educators.\"</p><p><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/ai-workshop-ciast-raspberry-pi-esp32-tvet/photo-1-2025-08-07-10-13-08.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></strong></p>&nbsp;We were also pleasantly surprised when CIAST asked about Raspberry Pi classroom kits and how these tools could be brought into competitions and long-term programs. That tells us this isn't just a one-off, it’s part of a bigger movement.&nbsp;\"I kept everything focused on small wins. Just getting an LED to blink from a gesture was a big moment.\"<p>Our trainer shared how the syllabus was built with simplicity in mind. We avoided overwhelming the group with jargon and instead focused on <strong>progressive learning</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>Understand the core concept</p></li><li><p>Get the hardware running</p></li><li><p>See it do something real</p></li><li><p>Reflect on where to apply it</p></li></ul><p>About 70% of the time was spent on hands-on, which made the learning stick. This is just the beginning.</p><p>We’re already planning similar workshops with other <strong>TVET institutions, polytechnics, and robotics groups</strong> across Malaysia. And we’re working on:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Plug-and-play AI kits</strong> for robotics, classrooms, and smart automation</p></li><li><p><strong>Curriculum-ready tutorials</strong> aligned with education goals</p></li><li><p>&nbsp;More collabs with those who share our mission to democratize AI</p></li></ul><p><em>\"We want AI to be as accessible as LEGO and just as fun to build with.\"</em></p><p>Raspberry Pi is only the start. We’re exploring drones, smart automation panels, and even voice-activated projects next.</p><h3>Want to Join the Journey?</h3><p>If you’re an instructor, trainer, or institution interested in bringing AI to your community, we’d love to hear from you. Reach out to us<a href=\"https://wa.me/+6045480668\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>&nbsp;or join our <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/cytrons-telegram-channel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Telegram Community</a> to stay in the loop. Let’s build the next generation of AI-powered makers from the classroom up.</p><p><a href=\"http://qr.link/aX8uQ7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/ai-workshop-ciast-raspberry-pi-esp32-tvet/raspberry-pi-telegram-1.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>"}, {"slug": "iriv-cm4-Vibration-Monitoring", "title": "Raspberry Pi Success Story: Real-Time Industrial Vibration Monitoring and Alert System Using IRIV", "date": "17 Jul 2025", "author": "HY Ng", "topic": "projects", "kind": "Customer project", "desc": "Real-Time Industrial Vibration Monitoring and Alert System Using IRIV PiControl for industrial IoT 4.0", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/industrial-thumbnail-13-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/industrial-thumbnail-13.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi in Industry"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 2GB RAM 16GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-2gb-ram-16gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W216/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,563.45", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 4GB RAM 32GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W432/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,799.70", "old": null}], "words": 488, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Real-Time Industrial Vibration Monitoring and Alert System Using IRIV&nbsp;PiControl&nbsp;- Mutiara Jayateknik Engineering Sdn Bhd</h2><p><b>Company Name</b>: Mutiara Jayateknik Engineering Sdn Bhd<br> <b>Website</b>:<a href=\"https://mutiaraengineering.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://mutiaraengineering.com/</a></p><p><br> Mutiara Jayateknik Engineering Sdn Bhd is a solutions-driven engineering company specialising in industrial automation, condition monitoring, and energy systems. We provide turnkey solutions that integrate sensors, controllers, and cloud platforms to improve industrial efficiency, reliability, and safety.</p><h2><b></b>What Problem Were You&nbsp;Solving?<b></b></h2><p>Many factories rely on periodic manual checks for vibration monitoring of critical machines, which increases the risk of undetected failures and costly downtimes. There was a need for a system that could provide continuous, real-time vibration data, along with early warning alerts, to prevent breakdowns and reduce maintenance costs.</p><h2>How Did You Solve the Problem?</h2><p>We developed a remote vibration monitoring system using the IRIV IO Controller and Wilcoxon 4–20 mA sensors. In this setup, the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> acts as the master, while the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-io-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV IO Controller</a> functions as the slave. The PiControl collects vibration signals from machines and transmits the data via MQTT to a cloud-based dashboard.</p><p>Key implementation features include:</p><ul><li>Real-time analog input reading from vibration sensors (e.g., Wilcoxon PC420 series).<br> </li><li>MQTT secure connection to HiveMQ Cloud.<br> </li><li>ESP32 &amp; website dashboard showing live current, velocity, waveform, and machine model.<br> </li><li>Firebase backend storing historical data and generating alerts.<br> </li><li>WebSocket for real-time updates on a local or remote interface.</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/3-iriv.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>What Is the Advantage of Your Solution/Application?</h2><ul><li>24/7 Remote Monitoring: Enables continuous machine condition tracking.</li><li>Real-Time Alerts: Immediate buzzer and dashboard alerts when thresholds are exceeded.</li><li>Reduced Downtime: Predictive maintenance reduces risk of sudden failure.</li><li>Cloud Integration: Easily integrates with MQTT, Firestore, and other cloud tools.</li><li>Field-Tested Deployment: System runs reliably in industrial environments using ruggedized IRIV hardware.</li></ul><h2>Key Highlights for the system:</h2><ul><li>Real-time data collection from 4-20mA vibration sensors.</li><li>Seamless MQTT integration with HiveMQ Cloud.</li><li>Firebase + WebSocket live dashboard (mobile + desktop view).</li><li>Long-press reset to restart monitoring mode.</li><li>Data archiving and automated daily reports via Firebase Cloud Functions.</li><li>Sensor inactivity alerts and condition tracking.</li><li>Easy integration with MQTT and sensors</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/4.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/5.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Comments:</h2><p>We are pleased with the flexibility and reliability of the IRIV PiControll and IRIV IO Controller, especially for edge deployment in remote or industrial settings. The platform’s GPIO, analog, and Ethernet support made integration with standard industrial sensors and MQTT infrastructure straightforward. Looking forward to expanding the solution across more facilities. </p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-vibration-monitoring/irivmutiara.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Brief introduction of IRIV PiControl:</h2><p><br> The IRIV PiControl is an industrial-grade controller designed for data acquisition, monitoring, and control applications. Powered by a Raspberry Pi Compute Module, it features multiple I/O ports, supports industrial protocols like Modbus and OPC UA, and enables integration with cloud platforms via MQTT. It's ideal for Industrial IoT (IIoT), automation, and smart factory solutions.</p><p>For more information about the system, please visit <a href=\"http://www.mqtt.com.my\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.mqtt.com.my</a></p><p>For more information about the IRIV PiControl, please visit<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol</a></p><p>If you have a use case you’d like to share with us, feel free to email us at: <a>myindustry@cytron.io</a>.</p>"}, {"slug": "iriv-cm4-smartfarming", "title": "Raspberry Pi Success Story: Empowering Modern Farming with IRIV PiControl - MyAgriTech System", "date": "18 Nov 2024", "author": "HY Ng", "topic": "projects", "kind": "Customer project", "desc": "Empowering Modern Farming Smart Farming with IRIV PiControl Powered by Raspberry Pi", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/industrial-thumbnail-6-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/industrial-thumbnail-6.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi in Industry"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 2GB RAM 16GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-2gb-ram-16gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W216/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,563.45", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 4GB RAM 32GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W432/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,799.70", "old": null}], "words": 777, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2><b>Empowering Modern Farming with IRIV PiControl&nbsp;- MyAgriTech System</b></h2><p>Farming today faces many challenges, including water shortages, unpredictable weather, and high labor costs. To help address these, MyAgriTech, an IoT solution that uses data and automation to help farmers manage their farms more efficiently. Initially, MyAgriTech used the ESP32 as the core of its system, but to keep up with modern farming needs, the team switched to the IRIV PiControl&nbsp;powered by the Raspberry Pi Compute Module 4 (CM4). This new controller provides more power and flexibility, making MyAgriTech’s solution even more effective.</p><h3>The Challenges with ESP32 in Modern Agriculture</h3><p>The ESP32 a popular microcontroller known for its affordability and basic functionality, served MyAgriTech well in the early stages of IoT agriculture. However, as farming became more complex and required more real-time data, automation, and remote monitoring, the ESP32 started to show its limits. It had trouble handling large amounts of data, running advanced calculations, and keeping a steady connection across large farm areas.</p><p>Farming today requires robust systems that capable of supporting a wide range of sensors, monitoring devices, and automated equipment. The complexity of modern agricultural processes, including precision irrigation, soil health monitoring, and crop management, required a controller that could process large data quickly and work reliably in different, sometimes harsh, environments. That’s where the IRIV, came in to meet these demands.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/photo-2024-11-18-18-19-42.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h3>The Benefits of IRIV in IoT Agriculture</h3><p>Switching to the IRIV controller has brought big improvements to MyAgriTech’s IoT solutions. Here are some of the main benefits:</p><ol><li>More Processing Power</li></ol><p>The Raspberry Pi CM4 has a much faster processor than the ESP32. With its strong ARM Cortex-A72 processor, the IRIV system can handle complex data analysis, run machine learning models, and manage multiple tasks at once. This makes it easier to automate and make better decisions on the farm.</p><ol><li>Improved Connectivity</li></ol><p>Modern farms need reliable connections between different devices. The IRIV system supports fast Ethernet, Wi-Fi, and Bluetooth, which keeps MyAgriTech’s IoT devices connected, even in remote areas where connectivity is usually challenging.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture3.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Different setup for IRIV PiControl&nbsp;based on different systems</p><ol><li>Scalability for Growing Farms</li></ol><p>As farms get bigger, their needs grow too. The IRIV system can easily expand, supporting a variety of sensors and devices. This makes it ideal for large farms, allowing farmers to set up IoT devices across wide areas—from soil sensors to climate monitors.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture4.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture5.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>On site environmental monitoring</p><ol><li>More Memory and Storage</li></ol><p>The Raspberry Pi CM4 offers more memory and storage space than the ESP32, which is essential for saving large amounts of data, like sensor readings and performance records. This extra storage allows MyAgriTech to keep and analyze long-term data, giving insights into crop health, water use, and farm productivity.</p><ol><li>Real-Time Monitoring and Control</li></ol><p>With the IRIV system, farmers can monitor key factors like soil moisture, temperature, and humidity in real-time. They can see live data, make quick decisions, and control systems like irrigation remotely, making farming more precise and efficient.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture6.png\" loading=\"lazy\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture7.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>GUI using Node-Red for real time local monitoring interface</p><p>Since transitioning to the IRIV PiControl, MyAgriTech has successfully installed several IoT systems across various farms, including monitoring, irrigation, and mixing systems. These systems have transformed how farmers manage their farms by providing:</p><ul><li><b>Monitoring system</b>: Continuous tracking of conditions like soil health, weather, and crop status. This gives farmers the information they need to improve their operations.</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture8.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture9.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Data insight and analysis from MyAgriTech platform</p><ul><li><b>Smart Irrigation</b>: Automated watering systems that adjust in real-time based on weather, soil moisture, and crop needs, helping to save water and increase crop yield.</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture10.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Smart Irrigation System</p><ul><li><b>Mixing Systems</b>: Automated nutrient-mixing systems that carefully blend fertilizers and other additives, keeping the soil healthy and plants growing well while reducing waste and costs.</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-cm4-smartfarming/picture11.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Automatic fertilizer mixing system</p><p>These systems help farmers manage resources more efficiently, grow more crops, and lower costs, while supporting more sustainable farming practices.</p><h3>Conclusion</h3><p><b></b><br> Switching from the ESP32 to the IRIV PiControl, powered by the Raspberry Pi CM4, has been a major step forward for MyAgriTech in using IoT technology to improve farming. With more processing power, better connectivity, and scalability, the IRIV system gives farmers a more reliable and advanced way to manage their farms. With successful monitoring, irrigation, and mixing systems now in place, MyAgriTech is helping farmers optimize their farms, save resources, and increase productivity. As agriculture relies more on technology, MyAgriTech’s innovations will continue to lead the way in making farming smarter and more sustainable.</p><p>For more information about MyAgriTech system, please visit <a href=\"https://www.myagri.tech/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.myagri.tech/</a></p><p>For more information about the IRIV PiControl, please visit<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol</a></p><p>If you have a use case you’d like to share with us, feel free to email us at:<a>myindustry@cytron.io</a>.</p><p><img src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/iriv-application-infographic.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>"}, {"slug": "jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience", "title": "My Experience Attending the NVIDIA Jetson Workshop by Cytron", "date": "04 Nov 2024", "author": "Rupa", "topic": "training", "kind": "Workshop", "desc": "Share my experience attending an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano workshop, learned about OpenCV, Docker, computer vision, and IoT integration using Blynk.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/kit-jn-ornn-tr-header-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/kit-jn-ornn-tr-header.png", "tags": ["NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano", "Workshop", "Computer Vision", "IoT", "Blynk", "AI Edge Computing"], "products": [{"name": "Nvidia Jetson Orin Nano Super Training Kit - AI Computer Vision", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-nvidia-jetson-orin-nano-training-kit-computer-vision", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/KIT-JN-ORNN-TR/traning-kit-super-268x268.jpg", "price": null, "old": null}], "words": 825, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2><strong>Introduction</strong></h2><p>Recently, I had the incredible opportunity to attend a workshop hosted by Cytron, focusing on the NVIDIA Jetson platform, specifically the Jetson Orin Nano. Led by <a href=\"https://www2.utar.edu.my/cv/index.jsp?cv=teohsk&amp;reqPageId=aboutMe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Dr. Teoh Shen Khang</a>, an assistant professor in the Faculty of Information and Communication Technology at UTAR. The workshop provided invaluable insights into cutting-edge technologies, including OpenCV, Docker, Computer Vision, and the Internet of Things (IoT), utilizing Blynk for IoT projects.</p><p>Here's a list of the specific topics discussed in this Workshop:</p><ul><li>Artificial Intelligence and Deep Learning Concepts</li><li>Get to Know Your Nvidia Jetson Orin Nano Developer Kit</li><li>Getting Started with your Nvidia Jetson Orin Nano Developer Kit</li><li>Using your Nvidia Jetson Orin Nano Developer Kit</li><li>Getting started with the jetson-inference Docker Container</li><li>Hands-on with Image Classification</li><li>Hands-on with Object Detection</li><li>Hands-on with Semantic Segmentation</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/img-2194-1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Dr. Teoh Shen Khang conducting the workshop.</p><h2><strong>Introduction&nbsp;To&nbsp;Jetson&nbsp;Orin&nbsp;Nano</strong></h2><p>The workshop began with an overview of the NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano, a powerful, compact computing platform designed for AI and machine learning applications. Dr. Teoh Shen Khang introduced us to the capabilities of the Orin Nano, emphasizing its efficiency in handling complex tasks while maintaining a low power consumption profile. This combination of performance and efficiency makes the Orin Nano an ideal choice for robotics, drones, and various IoT applications. This workshop focused on the Jetson Orin Nano Training Kit.&nbsp;If you are interested in getting a Jetson Orin Nano for yourself, head over to our page <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-nvidia-jetson-orin-nano-8gb-kits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/kit-jn-ornn-tr-a.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The Jetson Orin Nano Training Kit.</p><h2><strong>Understanding&nbsp;Docker</strong></h2><p>The next segment of the workshop introduced us to Docker, a platform that allows developers to automate the deployment of applications in lightweight, portable containers. Dr. Teoh explained the significance of Docker in the context of developing applications for the Jetson platform. We learned how to create Docker images and run containers, which simplified the process of managing dependencies and versions in our projects. This knowledge is crucial for developing scalable and maintainable applications, especially when working with AI and IoT systems. In this workshop, we used the <a href=\"https://github.com/dusty-nv/jetson-inference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jetson-Inference Docker</a>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/screenshot-2024-11-04-104646.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Sucessful Installation of the Jetson Inference Docker.</p><h2><strong>Diving&nbsp;Into&nbsp;OpenCV</strong></h2><p>One of the key components of the workshop was a hands-on session with OpenCV (Open Source Computer Vision Library). OpenCV is an essential tool for anyone working in the fields of computer vision and image processing. During the workshop, we learned how to utilize OpenCV for various applications, such as image recognition and object detection. Dr. Teoh guided us through several practical examples, illustrating how to manipulate images and analyze video streams in real-time. This experience provided a solid foundation for understanding how computer vision can be implemented in real-world scenarios.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/screenshot-2024-11-04-111217.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Reading an image using OpenCV</p><h2><strong>Applications&nbsp;In&nbsp;Computer&nbsp;Vision</strong></h2><p>As the workshop progressed, we delved deeper into specific applications of computer vision using the Jetson Orin Nano. Dr. Teoh demonstrated various algorithms for image processing, including facial recognition and object tracking. We explored how to implement these algorithms using OpenCV, enabling us to build intelligent applications that can interpret and respond to visual data. The interactive sessions allowed us to experiment with different Computer Vision Applications, fostering a hands-on learning environment.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/img-2204-1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Jetson Orin Nano with a <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-8mp-camera-module-v2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Raspberry Pi V2 camera</a> for Computer Vision Applications.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/screenshot-2024-11-04-102339.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Example of Computer Vision - Color Segmentation.</p><h2><strong>Integrating IoT With&nbsp;Blynk</strong></h2><p>Another exciting aspect of the workshop was the integration of IoT technologies using Blynk, a platform designed to simplify the development of IoT applications. Dr. Teoh showcased how Blynk can be utilized to create user interfaces for controlling devices and visualizing data from sensors. We learned how to connect our Jetson devices to the Blynk platform, enabling remote monitoring and control of our projects. This integration opened up new possibilities for building smart applications that can interact with the physical world.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/img-2236-1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Setup of the Jetson Orin Nano with IOT integration using Blynk platform.</p><h2><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2><p>Cytron’s commitment to fostering technology education was evident throughout the workshop. Cytron offers an educator’s discount on Jetson products, making it easier for teachers to access this cutting-edge technology. This discount is a fantastic opportunity for educators interested in bringing AI and IoT concepts into the classroom, allowing them to empower the next generation of tech enthusiasts. If you are an educator and are interested, do email our sales team (<a href=\"mailto:sales@cytron.io?subject=NVidia%20Educators%20Program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">sales@cytron.io</a>) or visit the link <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/nividia_educators_program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p><p>Attending the NVIDIA Jetson Workshop led by Dr. Teoh Shen Khang was a transformative experience that deepened my understanding of AI, computer vision, and IoT technologies. The hands-on approach and practical examples provided by Dr. Teoh made complex concepts accessible and engaging. I left the workshop not only with new knowledge but also with a sense of excitement about the future of technology and the potential applications of the NVIDIA Jetson platform.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/jetson-orin-nano-workshop-experience/img-2255-1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Group photo with all the participants.</p><p>I am grateful to Cytron Technologies&nbsp;for organizing this workshop and to Dr. Teoh for sharing his expertise. I look forward to applying what I’ve learned and continuing to explore the vast possibilities of AI and IoT.</p><p><a href=\"http://qr.codes/b2TBX5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/catalog/products/V-JN-NN4G/nvidia-jetson-telegram.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>"}, {"slug": "iriv-customization-nexoprima-cm4", "title": "Raspberry Pi CM4 Success Story: NexoPrima mCare for Labor Room Information System", "date": "12 Aug 2024", "author": "HY Ng", "topic": "projects", "kind": "Customer project", "desc": "NexoPrima mCare for Labor Room Information System Using NexoLink IoT Device Rpi Powered By CM4", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/iriv-customization-nexoprima-cm4/industrial-thumbnail-5-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-customization-nexoprima-cm4/industrial-thumbnail-5.png", "tags": [], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}], "words": 672, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>NexoPrima mCare is a Labour Room Information System that is designed to empower clinicians in monitoring and overseeing the well-being of both expectant mothers and newborns throughout the labor and delivery process.</p><h2><br> Challenges in the Labor Room</h2><p>The labor room presents numerous challenges that require precise and continuous monitoring to ensure the safety and well-being of both mothers and newborns:</p><ul><li>Complex Monitoring Requirements: Continuous tracking of vital signs and fetal heart rate is crucial, requiring reliable and accurate monitoring systems.</li><li>High-Stakes Decision-Making: Clinicians must make swift, informed decisions based on real-time data to address complications promptly.</li><li>Efficient Workflow Management: The need to balance patient care with extensive documentation can lead to inefficiencies and potential errors.</li><li>Data Integration: Integrating data from various medical devices and systems into a coherent, accessible format is a significant challenge.</li><li>Patient Prioritization: With multiple patients to manage, prioritizing care based on real-time data is critical to ensuring optimal outcomes.</li></ul><h2>Overview of the Advanced Labor Room Information System</h2><p>In the fast-paced and critical environment of maternity care, the need for precise, reliable, and continuous monitoring is paramount. NexoPrima’s Advanced Labor Room Information System, mCare, meets these needs by integrating state-of-the-art monitoring technologies with real-time data analytics and comprehensive surveillance capabilities. The system is designed to gather data from various CTG machines, plot graphs, display the data on a user-friendly dashboard, and implement AI learning for advanced analysis. This analysis is particularly focused on critical metrics such as fetal heart rate rhythm, contractions, and blood pressure.</p><p><meta><b><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcUPoyDGfaziC-8JzI-fLD4BvjEfbub_N6CR3sdfH5bI9MLXVCvuCVjh2kxNBitcIl80dg5z0tbPclY3NecxoP05ByHJrNAcM3LJUb-Z3WUEHYMQZdjh0mAlzd13Ol6wDFjqDtWAcfVmHc80i6y7GFbcCnF?key=rkY5scE0mRD-wFP3G6WZKQ\" loading=\"lazy\"></b></p><p><b>NexoLink IoT Device</b></p><p><meta></p><p><b><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXf4QyPNllwRsXssBdf2RJDe28fvzxXRWGrkBJP3GHW8xOuLhvYUuWD5t7_jkbmrot3rprLr8ps6VgKazQvoG8l6-XhrBWP_2RHKJl_-agy2uljT0GZE4lLMKRmRb1J0YYVkKMaFQiWYxJ4u1oJ63NEI2ac?key=rkY5scE0mRD-wFP3G6WZKQ\" loading=\"lazy\"></b></p><p><b>CTG machine</b></p><p><b><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXeftXjLTD0EXV9Yh6pYVNjRl7nLTgY35kYD4EKhCFJ5U98vJvG_jtSCkn-Ha8NKAw99iO9vMnDkynRZPbYKA56jNBIPe-EN7OU1EJUXfMII8bOillR0BBXYIXlyWcZ-Thq-LZPu2n3j-4dUlzRdpXX-I_s8?key=rkY5scE0mRD-wFP3G6WZKQ\" loading=\"lazy\"></b></p><p><b>Live data from the CTG machine will continuously be analyzed and classified in real-time in patient CTG view/monitoring.</b></p><p><b><img src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXcBOXsvtcPy3aYq30Dg2yH8t5jtsKQNdcfbusoJrejrbPI4mD8SHAlG41fjDGpzcvKm7H3XgYi6iLLlOAQfPYdrEutR6xLwr_1EREx72F1cHJf1hWQiwv2J9DNRdGdeofFzVNLk-BK6_00dQ7luJOy8nlks?key=rkY5scE0mRD-wFP3G6WZKQ\" loading=\"lazy\"></b></p><p><b>Bird’s eye view of multiple patients’ vital information from a single dashboard, thus making it easier to prioritize patients that need more attention.</b></p><h2><br> Advantages of the System</h2><ul><li>Minimizing Labor Risk: Continuous live CTG data charting and analysis with notification and alarm systems.</li><li>Prioritizing Patient Treatment: A bird’s eye view of multiple patients’ vital information from a single dashboard, making it easier to prioritize those needing more attention.</li><li>Auto Archive / Historical Data: CTG and patient data are stored in a central server and easily accessible at any time.</li><li>Remote Monitoring: The web-based solution allows monitoring anywhere within the hospital network or remotely.</li><li>Multiple CTG Vendor Support: NexoLink’s integration with various CTG vendors ensures broad compatibility and reliability.</li><li>Assisting Clinicians with Analytics: Real-time analytics and classification of CTG FHR data based on FIGO rules.</li></ul><h2>The Role of NexoLink</h2><p>NexoLink, a custom IoT device powered by Raspberry Pi CM4 connects to medical devices for data capture, enabling efficient and accurate data transfer across different systems.</p><p><br> <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-customization-nexoprima-cm4/mcare.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Custom Design by Cytron Technologies</h2><p><a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/agile-manufacturing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cytron Technologies</a> is collaborating with NexoPrima to design the hardware for the NexoLink IoT Device. By utilizing their IRIV Industrial 4.0 Pi Controller, which is powered by Raspberry Pi CM4 as the foundation, Cytron tailored the NexoLink device to meet the specific needs of NexoPrima’s mCare system. The IRIV controller’s robust capabilities in industrial automation and IoT applications provided a reliable platform for developing the NexoLink, ensuring seamless integration and high performance in a critical healthcare environment.<br> </p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>NexoPrima’s successful use of NexoLink in its Advanced Labor Room Information System is a big step forward in maternity care. By using modern technology and real-time data software, NexoPrima has improved patient safety and efficiency in labor rooms. This is yet another success story of our client using our custom IoT hardware device powered by the Raspberry Pi CM4. We wish them continued success.</p><p><meta></p><p>For more information about NexoPrima and the Advanced Labor Room Information System, please visit NexoPrima’s website <a href=\"https://www.nexoprima.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.nexoprima.com</a></p><p>For more information about the design and customization service provided by Cytron Technologies, please visit Cytron’s website <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://my.cytron.io/iriv-picontrol</a></p><p>If you have a use case you’d like to share with us, feel free to email us at:<a>myindustry@cytron.io</a></p><h2>Summary:</h2><p><a href=\"p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/iriv-application-infographic.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p><p><a href=\"p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> has shown the performance and endurance of Industrial edge controllers. The openness of its architecture, ready with Raspberry Pi OS, and support from many software makes it the perfect choice for this project.</p>"}, {"slug": "p-retrofitting-a-1mw-solar-famr-for-efficency-with-iriv-picontrol", "title": "Retrofitting a 1MW Solar Farm for Efficiency with IRIV PiControl", "date": "06 Feb 2024", "author": "Ober Choo", "topic": "projects", "kind": "Customer project", "desc": "Reviving a 1 MW Solar Farm with an IRIV PiControl, getting data from all 16 inverters, restrunning the data, and sending it to the cloud.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/p-retrofitting-a-1mw-solar-famr-for-efficency-with/industrial-thumbnail-12-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-retrofitting-a-1mw-solar-famr-for-efficency-with/industrial-thumbnail-12.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi in Industry"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}], "words": 432, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>By <a href=\"https://edas.my/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EDA Solutions</a></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-retrofitting-a-1mw-solar-famr-for-efficency-with/edas-solar-farm-j.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>The Challenge:</h2><p>A 1MW solar farm suffers from malfunctioning monitoring due to outdated 1MW solar inverters reaching the end of their support lifespan. This hinders critical data collection and impairs efficient operation and maintenance (O&amp;M).</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-retrofitting-a-1mw-solar-famr-for-efficency-with/edas-solar-farm-i.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The 1 MW Solar Farm</p><h2>The Solution:</h2><p>A clever retrofit, powered by open-source technologies, breathes new life into the system. Here's how:</p><ul><li>Custom <a href=\"https://nodered.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Node-RED</a>: A bespoke Node-RED is developed to specifically acquire serial data, matching the unique data structure and format of the Kaco Powador inverters. Node-RED is a visual programming tool, perfect for building custom data flows.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl powered by Raspberry Pi CM4</a>: The custom program (Node-RED) runs on an Industrial Controller, a compact yet powerful IR4.0 Edge Controller developed by Cytron Technologies. The IRIV-PiControl comes with comprehensive Industrial interfaces. For example, the fully isolated RS485 and RS232 ports. Fully Isolated Digital Inputs and Outputs, and Analogue inputs. IRIV PiControl also features dual RJ45/Ethernet Ports, making it ideal for internal machine communication and providing an additional Ethernet port for Internet access. This cost-effective and versatile platform handles data acquisition with ease.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://mqtt.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MQTT</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://grafana.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grafana</a> Cloud: The extracted data is fed via MQTT, a lightweight messaging protocol, to the Grafana Cloud platform. Grafana excels at data visualisation and observability, enabling real-time monitoring and performance insights.</li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-retrofitting-a-1mw-solar-famr-for-efficency-with/edas-solar-farm-b.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The IRIV PiControl as the Gateway to collect data from Solar Inverters via RS485</p><h2>The Benefits:</h2><ul><li><strong>Data Continuity:</strong> The new system seamlessly replaces the outdated monitoring, ensuring uninterrupted data collection.</li><li><strong>Enhanced Efficiency:</strong>&nbsp;Real-time monitoring empowers informed O&amp;M decisions, optimising performance and maximising energy output.</li><li><strong>Cost-Effectiveness:</strong> Leveraging open-source tools and Raspberry Pi minimises hardware costs compared to proprietary solutions.</li><li><strong>Future-Proofing:</strong> The modular design enables scalability and facilitates the easy integration of future upgrades.</li></ul><h2>The Impact:</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-retrofitting-a-1mw-solar-famr-for-efficency-with/edas-solar-farm-h.jpeg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>There are 16 Inverters and are all connected to IRV PiControl’s RS485 port in a daisy-chain topology</p><p>This retrofit demonstrates the power of open-source solutions and innovative thinking in revitalising ageing solar infrastructure. By extending the lifespan of existing equipment and improving O&amp;M efficiency, this project contributes to a more sustainable and cost-effective solar future. The data collected from each inverter is:</p><ul><li>Power of AC (Alternating Current)</li><li>Power Factor, Q of AC</li><li>Current, I of AC</li><li>Voltage, V of AC</li><li>Energy of AC</li><li>Status of the inverter</li></ul><p>All this data is then restructured to be the Kaco Powador telemetry format and fed to the cloud.</p><h2>Summary:</h2><p><a href=\"p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/iriv-application-infographic.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p><p><a href=\"p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> has shown the performance and endurance of Industrial edge controllers. The openness of its architecture, ready with Raspberry Pi OS, and support from many software make it the perfect choice for this project.</p>"}, {"slug": "p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc", "title": "IRIV PiControl as IoT Gateway at SHRDC (Selangor Human Resource Development Center)", "date": "29 Dec 2023", "author": "Ober Choo", "topic": "projects", "kind": "Customer project", "desc": "SHRDC is now using IRIV PiControl in their IR4.0 IoT Gateway workshop. They have also built a Controller Box with a proper power supply, IRIV PiControl, LED indicators, Switches", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/industrial-thumbnail-11-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/industrial-thumbnail-11.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi in Industry"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 2GB RAM 16GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-2gb-ram-16gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W216/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,563.45", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 4GB RAM 32GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W432/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,799.70", "old": null}], "words": 614, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>By <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shyanchua\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Dr. Chua Wen-shyan</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.shrdc.org.my/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Selangor Human Resource Development Centre</a> or SHRDC is a not-for-profit training and talent development centre established by the industry and government in 1992 to appropriately skill Malaysians for a sustained and addressable pool of high-impact talents for companies and businesses.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/where-iriv-is-mounted.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>IRIV as the IoT Gateway</h2><p>The training kit utilises the<a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a>&nbsp;as a data acquisition device and an IoT gateway.&nbsp;It performs the following functions:</p><ul><li>Data Acquisition:<ul><li>Receives signals from switches and RS485 sensors.</li><li>These signals can be individually collected or grouped (e.g., all switch signals, all LED signals, etc.).</li><li>So far, no pre-processing of data has been done before logging. Nonetheless, this can be done if needed to formulate the necessary key parameters for monitoring machine, process, and/or production efficiency and effectiveness.</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li>Data Transmission:<ul><li>Sends received data to both the laptop/computer and the cloud for logging.</li><li>Uses a wireless connection (WiFi) for communication with the laptop/computer.</li><li>IRIV PiControl provides the flexibility of connection to the Internet and machines. With dual Ethernet ports, we can utilise one for Internet access and send data to the cloud. Another Ethernet port for a Machine interface, like<a href=\"https://www.wevolver.com/article/understanding-modbus-tcp-ip-an-in-depth-exploration\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Modbus TCP/IP</a>.</li><li>In some cases, WiFi/Wireless connections are not permitted in manufacturing facilities; the dual Ethernet ports come in handy!</li></ul></li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/shrdc-iriv-overview.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Overview of SHRDC Training Kit with IRIV PiControl</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/the-overall-view-of-the-poc-kit.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The Actual Training Kit</p><p>The training kit is assembled in a plastic enclosure with a transparent top cover. There are two DIN Rails for equipment mounting and proper wire trunking. The transparent cover provides visibility of the whole system and also the status of some devices (for example, LED indicators on PSU, IRIV PiControl, and also on the Relay modules)</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/left-side-connection-for-digital-input-and-output.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"><br> </p><p>The IRIV PiControl is mounted on DIN Rail, powered by a 24VDC Meanwell PSU (also DIN Rail mountable).&nbsp; All wires are terminated with the ferrule, and the 24VDC is labeled properly.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/wire-connection-for-the-led-switches-and-rs485.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The switches (Digital Input to IRIV PiControl) and LED indicators (Digital Output from IRIV PiControl) are mounted on the transparent cover. There is also an emergency switch that will cut off the 24VDC supply to IRIV PiControl.<br> </p><h2>Node-RED as the Software Platform</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/printscreen-node-reda.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The training kit relies on <a href=\"https://nodered.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Node-RED</a> for its software functionality. This choice was made due to the following reasons:</p><ul><li>Continuity: Node-RED was previously used for data pulling and pushing in their current gateway. Maintaining consistency in the methodology simplifies the implementation and introduction of IRIV to the industry and community.</li><li>Ease of Use: Node-RED offers a user-friendly visual programming interface, making it suitable for beginners and experienced users.</li></ul><h2>Signal Flow and Programming</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/dashboard.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>The project separates signal flow and programming into two distinct domains:</p><ul><li>Signal Flow:<ul><li>Switches to Cloud: Switch signals are directly sent to the cloud for logging.</li><li>The same goes for the status of LED, it is logged into the cloud too.</li></ul></li><li>Programming:<ul><li>However, the logic for switching signals and how the LED works is programmed locally on the laptop/computer. This allows for flexible modification without affecting the nodes in IRIV PiControl.</li></ul></li></ul><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/p-iriv-picontrol-as-iot-gateway-at-shrdc/printscreen-node-redb.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Local programming provides advantages:</p><ul><li>Flexibility: You can easily modify the programming for switches and LEDs without needing to reconfigure IRIV PiControl or the Cloud.</li><li>Convenience: Programming can be done directly on the laptop/computer, eliminating the need for additional hardware or software.</li></ul><p>However:</p><ul><li>MQTT Broker Dependence: An MQTT broker is required to establish communication between IRIV PiControl and the laptop/computer.</li><li>WiFi Requirement: WiFi connectivity is necessary for communication between IRIV PiControl and the laptop/computer.</li></ul><h2>Learning Outcomes:</h2><p><a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/iriv-application-infographic.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p><p>Participants will learn about:</p><ul><li>The basic setup of IRIV PiControl - hardware and software.</li><li>MQTT Protocol: The MQTT protocol facilitates communication between devices in an IoT ecosystem.</li><li>Cloud Data Logging: Understand how data is collected and stored in the cloud for further analysis and visualisation.</li></ul>"}, {"slug": "industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-industrial-automation", "title": "Industry 4.0 Training Kit: Embracing the Future of Industrial Automation", "date": "14 Dec 2023", "author": "Ober Choo", "topic": "training", "kind": "Training kit", "desc": "Swinburne University - Sarawak has adopted IRIV PiControl into the Industry 4.0 Training Kit to futureproof the automation and industry training.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-in/industrial-thumbnail-10-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-in/industrial-thumbnail-10.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi in Industry"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 2GB RAM 16GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-2gb-ram-16gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W216/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,563.45", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl CM4 Wireless 4GB RAM 32GB eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/IRIV-PICL-W432/cm4-side-view-2-1000x1000-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,799.70", "old": null}], "words": 509, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>By <a href=\"https://www.swinburne.edu.my/staff/dr-hudyjaya-siswoyo-jo.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ir. Dr. Hudyjaya Siswoyo Jo</a></p><p>As we move towards Industry 4.0, the need for seamlessly integrated and intelligent systems in manufacturing becomes more critical than ever. This is where the Industry 4.0 Training Kit comes in, providing a hands-on learning experience for students in the Robotics &amp; Mechatronics Engineering program at <a href=\"https://www.swinburne.edu.my/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Swinburne Sarawak</a>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-in/industry4-training-kit.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>System Overview:</h2><p>The PLC in this Industry 4.0 Kit is in charge of Operational Technology, interfacing actuators, and sensors. The IRIV PiControl will be the IoT Gateway. There is also a HMI (Human Machine Interface) for real-time system status display. All these three main controllers are interconnected via a network switch, using Ethernet cables.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-in/industry4-training-kit-overview.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-in/industry4-training-kit-overview2.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>Bridging the Gap Between Industrial Automation and Data:</h2><p><a href=\"p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-in/iriv-picontrol-inbox.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p><p>The core of this training kit is the <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a>, a versatile device with dual functionality:</p><ul><li>IoT Gateway: <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> acts as a bridge between the factory automation system's programmable logic controller (PLC) and the connected cloud or local storage. This enables real-time data extraction and exchange, providing critical insights into production processes.</li><li>Edge Processor: Equipped with OpenCV and Python, <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a> transforms into an edge processor capable of performing basic machine vision tasks. This opens up possibilities for simple counting, quality inspection, and other image-based automation applications, directly on the factory floor.</li></ul><h2>Software Stack:</h2><p>To power this multifaceted functionality, the training kit utilises:</p><ul><li>Node.js and <a href=\"https://nodered.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Node-RED</a>: These JavaScript-based platforms provide a user-friendly environment for building complex IoT applications, handling data flows, and visualising real-time information.</li><li><a href=\"https://opencv.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenCV</a> with Python: This powerful combination equips IRIV PiControl with machine vision capabilities, enabling image processing, feature detection, and object recognition within the edge computing framework.</li></ul><h2>Data Storage and Accessibility:</h2><p>The training kit offers flexibility in data storage, catering to both cloud and local needs. This ensures data availability for analysis and decision-making, whether real-time monitoring or offline investigation. IRIV PiControl is a good candidate as a local server too. It can expand the storage by adding an M.2 NVMe SSD (manual installation is needed).</p><h2>Future-Proofing Education:</h2><p><a href=\"p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/industry-4-training-kit-embracing-the-future-of-in/iriv-picontrol-view-a.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p><p>The Industry 4.0 Training Kit is designed to equip students with the essential skills and knowledge necessary to thrive in the rapidly evolving landscape of industrial automation. With a focus on cutting-edge technologies like IoT, edge computing, and machine vision, this training program bridges the gap between theoretical understanding and practical application, preparing students for success in the Industry 4.0 workforce.</p><h2>Timeline and Availability:</h2><p>Currently in the design stage, the Industry 4.0 Training Kit is scheduled for delivery in 2025, primarily catering to the <strong>Robotics &amp; Mechatronics Engineering program</strong> at Swinburne Sarawak. This innovative training platform will be housed in the Robotics Lab, providing students with a dedicated environment for hands-on learning and experimentation.</p><h2>Conclusion:</h2><p><a href=\"p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/iriv-application-infographic.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p><p>The Industry 4.0 Training Kit represents a significant step forward in engineering education, equipping students with the tools and knowledge necessary to contribute to the future of intelligent manufacturing. By integrating industrial-ready, open-platform edge controllers like <a href=\"https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-wireless-4gb-ram-32gb-emmc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">IRIV PiControl</a>, this training program lays the groundwork for a new generation of engineers equipped to navigate the complexities and opportunities of Industry 4.0.</p><p><a href=\"https://qr.link/BXAybc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/iriv-picontrol-industrial-grade-sim7600g-h-4g-dtu/raspberry-pi-for-professional-footer.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><br> </p>"}, {"slug": "raspberry-pi-success-stories-across-industries", "title": "Raspberry Pi Success Stories Across Industries", "date": "01 Sep 2023", "author": "Abdulrahman Alhamed", "topic": "rpi", "kind": "Insight", "desc": "In this article, we take you on a journey through the remarkable achievements made possible by the Raspberry Pi", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/raspberry-pi-success-stories-across-industries/thumbnail-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-success-stories-across-industries/thumbnail.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Raspberry Pi 5 Single Board Computer", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-5", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-RASPBERRY-PI-5/v-raspberry-pi-5-main-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM202.00++", "old": null}], "words": 734, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi has emerged as a true game-changer across industries. From factories to healthcare, and hospitality to digital signage, its impact has gone beyond limits and rewritten success stories. In this article, we take you on a journey through the remarkable achievements made possible by the Raspberry Pi. Join us as we explore how this unassuming single-board computer has ignited innovation and reshaped possibilities in a wide array of sectors.</p><h2>Brompton</h2><p><div class=\"ia-video\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Dh2Awd_0jh0\" loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Video\" loading=\"lazy\" allow=\"accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe></div></p><p><strong>Brompton</strong>, famous for their innovative folding bicycles, has embraced the power of Raspberry Pi in its London-based factory to make their success even bigger. They faced a challenge: keeping track of their production as more people wanted their bikes. So, they brought in Raspberry Pi computers to help out. Starting in 2013 with a line of nine production stations, they later expanded to 16 to meet increased demand, ultimately requiring more efficient tracking and monitoring capabilities.</p><p>Over a hundred Raspberry Pi devices, including Raspberry Pi 4 and earlier models, have been deployed across Brompton's factory. These devices play diverse roles, from monitoring pre-assembly and production lines to ensuring air quality control. The Raspberry Pi computers on production stations actively scan bicycle serial numbers, enabling real-time tracking of each unit's assembly progress. This data is leveraged for multiple purposes, such as providing assembly instructions to staff through connected displays, automating plate design for laser-etching machines, and assisting staff in meeting time targets through LED indicators.</p><h2>Bio Business</h2><p><img alt=\"\"></p><p><strong>Bio Business</strong> hit a challenge when they aimed to produce IoT monitoring devices for big companies like Siemens, GE, and Philips. These devices required precise environmental measurements like temperature and air quality for patients. But making all these devices connect to the cloud was a complex task. The company needed to remotely monitor machines like MRIs and CT scanners while ensuring a consistent supply of components for their expanding portfolio.</p><p>Bio Business turned to Raspberry Pi Compute Module 4 and RP2040 microcontrollers. Their CPAP device, which aids in maintaining a patient's airway, utilized RP2040 to monitor oxygen levels and manage power inputs and pressure sensors. Additionally, they introduced a Raspberry Pi-based oxygen concentrator that efficiently utilizes ambient air for oxygen supply, allowing users to adjust the flow.</p><p>By using Raspberry Pi technology, Bio Business not only overcame obstacles in production and connectivity but also became leaders in bringing together medical equipment and smart technology like IoT.</p><h2>KwickPOS</h2><p><img alt=\"\"></p><p><strong>KwickPOS</strong>, a Houston-based venture founded by tech enthusiasts Tom Jin and Ming Ye, began its journey in 2003 by crafting a Linux-based point-of-sale system for a Chinese restaurant. The success of their innovation spread quickly, leading to a transition into a full-fledged business in 2015. However, they encountered challenges. The issue lay in the expensive Windows systems, which were both prone to theft and occupied a lot of space. KwickPOS found a breakthrough with Raspberry Pi, using it to create discreet yet powerful terminals for restaurants. Their browser-based POS system, backed by Raspberry Pi servers, offered offline functionality—a crucial advantage in areas with internet disruptions. This resilience not only made them stand out but also made them better in the competition.</p><h2>Yodeck</h2><p><img alt=\"\"></p><p><strong>Yodeck </strong>has become a thriving participant in the global digital signage market, projected to reach $45 billion by 2030. CEO Vangelis Mihalopoulos initially ventured into the market with a PC-based offering, but struggled to find widespread success. Challenges arose from the high cost and limited scalability of their solution.</p><p>Recognizing the need for a more efficient and adaptable approach, Mihalopoulos and his team turned to Raspberry Pi. They crafted a Python-based application to run on Raspberry Pi, effectively managing content playback, scheduling, and device management. This allowed Yodeck to create an affordable yet powerful digital signage platform that automatically pushed content to client devices, ensuring consistent messaging across various displays and locations.</p><p>This innovation was driven by Mihalopoulos' insight into the industry's requirements and Raspberry Pi's impressive capabilities. By leveraging Raspberry Pi's flexibility and performance, Yodeck successfully established a reliable and cost-effective digital signage solution for clients ranging from large corporations to local businesses, solidifying their position in the competitive market.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi's impact knows no bounds. From factories to healthcare and beyond, its success stories illuminate the path to a more innovative future, where possibilities are limitless. So, stay tuned for the remarkable possibilities that technology like the Raspberry Pi can bring to our world!</p><h3>References:</h3><ol><li><a>Brompton</a></li><li><a>Bio Business</a></li><li><a>KwickPOS</a></li><li><a>Yodeck</a></li></ol><p><a href=\"http://qr.link/aX8uQ7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-success-stories-across-industries/raspberry-pi-telegram-1.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>"}, {"slug": "raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation", "title": "Raspberry Pi's Impact on Manufacturing Automation", "date": "21 Aug 2023", "author": "Abdulrahman Alhamed", "topic": "rpi", "kind": "Insight", "desc": "In this article, we're diving into how the Raspberry Pi is making its mark in manufacturing automation. We'll talk about how it's simplifying processes, ensure quality control, and enable real-time mo", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation/Thumbnail-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation/Thumbnail.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi", "Raspberry Pi in Industry"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Raspberry Pi 5 Single Board Computer", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-5", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-RASPBERRY-PI-5/v-raspberry-pi-5-main-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM202.00++", "old": null}], "words": 482, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the world of manufacturing, things are always moving ahead. Technology has become a key player in boosting how much we can make, cutting down on times when machines aren't running, and making everything run more efficiently. One piece of tech that's been turning heads lately is the Raspberry Pi. It started out as a tiny, budget-friendly computer meant for learning, but it's gone beyond that now. It's found its place in various industries, manufacturing included. In this article, we're diving into how the Raspberry Pi is making its mark in manufacturing automation. We'll talk about how it's simplifying processes, ensure quality control, and enable real-time monitoring. All of this adds up to better production and less time wasted.</p><h2>Process Automation</h2><p><img alt=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation/1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>(Photo source:<a>information-age</a>)</p><p>Raspberry Pi's compact size, low cost, and versatility make it an ideal candidate for process automation in manufacturing. With its GPIO pins and compatibility with various sensors and actuators, Raspberry Pi can be configured to control and manage different aspects of production lines. For instance, it can be used to control production line equipment, conveyor systems, machines and robots, ensuring consistent and accurate operations. This reduces the need for manual intervention, minimising human errors and enhancing production throughput.</p><h2>Quality Control</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation/2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"><img alt=\"\"></p><p>(Photo source:<a>Adafruit</a>)</p><p>Maintaining product quality is vitally important in manufacturing. Raspberry Pi can be equipped with various advanced sensors and cameras to perform real-time quality inspections. This enables the detection of defects, irregularities, or variations in products. By integrating the smart algorithms, Raspberry Pi can quickly analyze sensors data and make immediate decisions, preventing substandard products from entering the market. This results in cost savings, higher customer satisfaction, and a stronger brand reputation.</p><h2>Real-time Monitoring</h2><p><img alt=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation/3.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>(Photo source:<a>adlinktech</a>)</p><p>Monitoring manufacturing processes in real-time is crucial for identifying bottlenecks, inefficiencies, and potential breakdowns. Raspberry Pi's computational power allows it to gather data from various sensors placed across the production floor. This data can be analyzed and visualized using software tools, providing insights into the status of machines, temperature, humidity, and other relevant parameters, in order to achieve preventive maintenance in the production floor. By identifying patterns and anomalies, manufacturers can take proactive measures to prevent disruptions and optimize resource allocation.</p><h2>Reduced Downtime</h2><p><img alt=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation/4.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>(Photo source:<a>soracom</a>)</p><p>Unplanned downtime can be a significant drain on manufacturing productivity. Raspberry Pi can aid in predictive maintenance by continuously collecting data from sensors embedded in machinery. Through machine learning algorithms, patterns of behavior that indicate impending failures can be identified. This enables maintenance teams to perform repairs or replacements before a breakdown occurs, reducing costly downtime and improving overall equipment effectiveness (OEE).</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Raspberry Pi's applications are diverse and impactful. By integrating this technology into manufacturing automation, industries can expect improved productivity, enhanced product quality, and optimized resource utilization. As the manufacturing landscape continues to evolve, Raspberry Pi demonstrates the potential of innovative technologies in reshaping traditional industries.</p><p><a href=\"http://qr.link/aX8uQ7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/raspberry-pi-impact-on-manufacturing-automation/raspberry-pi-telegram-1.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>"}, {"slug": "from-education-to-industry-the-transformation-of-raspberry-pi", "title": "From Education to Industry: The Transformation of Raspberry Pi", "date": "12 Aug 2023", "author": "Abdulrahman Alhamed", "topic": "rpi", "kind": "Insight", "desc": "This article explores how the Raspberry Pi has evolved from a tool for hobbyists to a valuable resource in industrial settings.", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/from-education-to-industry-the-transformation-of-r/1-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/from-education-to-industry-the-transformation-of-r/1.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi"], "products": [{"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Raspberry Pi 5 Single Board Computer", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-5", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-RASPBERRY-PI-5/v-raspberry-pi-5-main-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM202.00++", "old": null}], "words": 1005, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In recent years, a small yet remarkable technology has gained significant importance in various industries – the Raspberry Pi. Initially designed as a low-cost computer for learning, the Raspberry Pi has expanded its reach to various industrial uses. This article explores how the Raspberry Pi has evolved from a tool for hobbyists to a valuable resource in industrial settings.</p><h2>The Journey of Raspberry Pi</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/from-education-to-industry-the-transformation-of-r/2.png\" loading=\"lazy\"><img alt=\"\"></p><p>Let's talk about how the Raspberry Pi went from being a tool for learning in schools to being really useful in big industries. Initially, the Raspberry Pi served as a small computer companion for students. It was small, didn't use much energy, and helped kids learn about computers and programming. But then, something interesting happened.</p><p>People realised that the Raspberry Pi could do more than just help students learn. It had some special qualities that made it a good fit for large industries as well. They created tougher versions of it, such as the Compute Module series, so it could handle the demanding tasks industries required.</p><p>Factories and businesses recognised that the Raspberry Pi could help them operate more efficiently. It began to perform tasks such as controlling machines in factories and maintaining remote equipment. The Raspberry Pi's ability to connect to the internet proved particularly useful. It helped gather data in real-time, meaning it happened right when it was happening. This data helped industries make smart decisions.</p><p>So, what used to be a friend to students in classrooms became a big help in industries. As the Raspberry Pi continues to improve, it demonstrates that it's not just for school, but also for the broader world of work.</p><h2>Industrial Integration of the Raspberry Pi</h2><p><img alt=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/from-education-to-industry-the-transformation-of-r/3.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>As the Raspberry Pi improved, it naturally found its way into commercial and small industrial ventures, thanks to its growing abilities. Its different parts are smoothly integrated into various digital devices, such as cameras, media players, communication tools, and portable music synthesisers. It has even found applications in unique areas, such as automating homes and recording data on the International Space Station. Many companies recognised this potential and took advantage of it by embedding Raspberry Pi modules into their industrial automation systems.</p><p>However, the major step into industries happened when they released the first Raspberry Pi Compute Module in 2014. After the regular Raspberry Pi gained popularity among everyday users, they began creating new versions specifically for businesses. They gathered all the essential components of the Raspberry Pi and placed them on a small board that could easily fit into a special slot.</p><p>The Compute Module was intended for integration into specialised PCBs or carrier boards designed for specific purposes. This provided hardware designers with more flexibility in shaping their physical dimensions, and engineers with expanded options for input/output (I/O) connections. Industries could adapt the Raspberry Pi Compute Module to meet their particular requirements. In later versions, it could be conveniently plugged into a USB port or mounted onto a DIN rail, showcasing its impressive versatility.</p><h2>How Is Raspberry Pi Used In Industry?</h2><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/from-education-to-industry-the-transformation-of-r/4.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"><img alt=\"\"></p><p>The versatile nature of the Raspberry Pi has led to its widespread adoption across various industrial applications, transforming the way businesses operate and innovate. From manufacturing floors to remote installations, the Raspberry Pi finds utility in various ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Automation and Control Systems</strong>: Raspberry Pi serves as a reliable control centre for industrial automation, overseeing machinery and processes. It facilitates real-time monitoring, data collection, and precise control adjustments, thereby enhancing efficiency and reducing the need for human intervention.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Internet of Things (IoT) Solutions</strong>: With its connectivity features, Raspberry Pi becomes a key component in IoT ecosystems. It seamlessly collects data from sensors and devices, enabling businesses to make informed decisions based on real-time insights.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Quality Control</strong>: Raspberry Pi's image processing capabilities aid in quality assessment. It can analyse visual data from production lines to identify defects and anomalies, ensuring products meet high standards.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Data Logging and Analysis</strong>: Industries rely on data to optimise operations. Raspberry Pi excels at gathering and analysing data in real-time, helping businesses monitor performance, identify trends, and make data-driven decisions.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Remote Monitoring and Management</strong>: The ability to connect to networks makes the Raspberry Pi an ideal tool for remotely monitoring assets. Industries with distributed infrastructure, such as utilities and oil rigs, use it to track equipment health, predict maintenance needs, and prevent downtime.</li></ul><p>The adaptable nature of Raspberry Pi ensures that its applications in industry are not limited to a predefined set. Its open-source community, vast software libraries, and customizable hardware interfaces empower industries to tailor solutions to their unique requirements. As technology continues to evolve, so does the role of Raspberry Pi in shaping innovative approaches across diverse industrial sectors.</p><h2>The Future of Raspberry Pi in Industry</h2><p><img alt=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/from-education-to-industry-the-transformation-of-r/5.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><p>Looking ahead, the Industrial <a>Raspberry Pi market is projected to expand</a>, with a forecasted size of $385 million by 2026, growing at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 15.7% from 2021 to 2026.</p><p>Several factors contribute to this growth. The preference for wireless networking devices in industries, combined with Raspberry Pi's role in industrial protocols and the adoption of IoT, drives this trend. Moreover, as industries embrace automation and intelligent warehousing, the Raspberry Pi's influence is set to expand further.</p><p>The road ahead holds exciting possibilities. Raspberry Pi's ability to enable IoT-connected devices, streamline processes, and guide data-driven decisions will continue to grow. As industries adopt automation and tap into IoT benefits, the Raspberry Pi's compact computing power will prove pivotal in enhancing efficiency, cost-effectiveness, and innovation. This ongoing trajectory emphasises the lasting importance of Raspberry Pi as a transformative tool in the industrial landscape.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Raspberry Pi's journey from a hobby tool to an industrial game-changer is truly remarkable. Its versatility in automation, IoT, and data analysis has changed how industries work. As the industrial Raspberry Pi market continues to grow due to wireless networking, IoT, and automation, its impact will only become stronger. Raspberry Pi's role in making industries efficient and innovative is a clear sign of its importance in shaping the future.</p>"}, {"slug": "9-reasons-why-industry-started-to-adopt-raspberry-pi", "title": "9 Reasons Why Industry Started to Adopt Raspberry Pi", "date": "02 Feb 2023", "author": "Yo Nutchanon", "topic": "rpi", "kind": "Insight", "desc": "In summary, the key advantages of the Raspberry Pi computers are their low cost, reliability, and comprehensive ecosystem. These factors have allowed them to secure a significant share in the market", "cover": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/tutorial/pi-in-industrial/industrial-thumbnail-3-320x180.png", "hero": "https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/pi-in-industrial/industrial-thumbnail-3.png", "tags": ["Raspberry Pi", "CM4", "edgebox", "pi4", "Raspberry Pi"], "products": [{"name": "reTerminal - RPi CM4 4G RAM 32GB and 5-Inch Cap Multi-Touch Screen", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-reterminal-rpi-cm4-and-5-inch-cap-multi-touch-screen", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/CM4-RET-W432/CM4%204GB-268x268.png", "price": "RM1,295.00", "old": null}, {"name": "IRIV PiControl - IR4.0 Industrial Controller", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-iriv-picontrol-cm4-industrial-controller", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-IRIV-PICONTROL/v-iriv-picontrol-main-3-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM1,489.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Raspberry Pi 5 Single Board Computer", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-5", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-RASPBERRY-PI-5/v-raspberry-pi-5-main-268x268.jpg", "price": "RM202.00++", "old": null}, {"name": "Raspberry Pi CM5 with Wireless - Pick RAM and eMMC", "url": "https://my.cytron.io/p-raspberry-pi-cm5-with-wireless-pick-ram-and-emmc", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/V-CM5-W/v-cm5-w-b-268x268.png", "price": "RM323.80++", "old": null}, {"name": "EdgeBox RPi 200 - Industrial Edge Controller", "url": "javascript:return false;", "img": "https://static.cytron.io/image/cache/catalog/products/EDGEBOX%20RPI%20200/1-102991599_edgebox-rpi-200-first(2)-268x268.jpg", "price": null, "old": null}], "words": 499, "useCase": false, "body": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi computers were originally developed for educational purposes in the United Kingdom, but have become increasingly popular for industrial applications in recent years. According to Raspberry Pi, tens of thousands of applications across various industries worldwide are powered by these computers. The increasing interest from enterprises and industries is due to a variety of reasons, which we will be exploring today. Here are <strong>9 possible reasons for their success in the industrial market</strong>.</p><h2>1. Value for Money</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi is considered a low-cost alternative for building automation and industrial control systems. In comparison to traditional industrial control tools like PLCs, it can perform the same tasks at a significantly lower cost.</p><h2>2. Flexibility</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi is versatile and can run on different platforms, including Linux and Windows IoT, and can be programmed in various languages, such as Python, C++, and Java. This versatility makes it easy to integrate with existing systems, such as PLCs, and makes it an ideal choice for building automation solutions.</p><h2>3. Compact Size</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi is a compact Single Board Computer, making it easy to install in tight spaces. With the ability to attach extra peripherals directly on the board, called \"Hardware attached on top\" (HAT), the entire system is compact and organized.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/pi-in-industrial/03.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>4. Durability</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi is a durable device that can withstand harsh industrial conditions and operate 24/7 in a wide range of temperature environments. It also has low power consumption.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/9-reasons-why-industry-started-to-adopt-raspberry-pi/iriv-pi-control-a-v2-800x800.png\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>5. Open Source Software</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi runs on open source software, enabling a large developer community to contribute to its development. This results in a more stable and efficient system and allows for customization of the software to meet individual user needs.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/pi-in-industrial/05.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>6. Easy to program</h2><p>You can easily code your Raspberry Pi with many Computer languages. Such as Python, C++, and more. Make you able to develop many types of applications.</p><h2>7. Rich IO Interfaces</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi is equipped with a range of interfaces, including Ethernet, USB, HDMI, 40-GPIO, CSI, and DSI, allowing for connection to various peripherals.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/pi-in-industrial/07.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>8. Universal USB-C Power</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi operates at 5V and can be powered through the USB C port, with a maximum current of 3A, making it easy to power the device.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/pi-in-industrial/08.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p><h2>9. Scalability</h2><p>The Raspberry Pi is suitable for both simple and complex projects. It can be operated as a standalone unit or as a cluster of multiple boards for increased power. The ability to scale from small to large makes it ideal for applications that require gradual system development over time.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>In summary, the key advantages of the Raspberry Pi computers are their low cost, reliability, and comprehensive ecosystem. These factors have allowed them to secure a significant share in the industrial computer market. If you need Raspberry Pi solutions for your project, our experts are available for consultation. We have ample support to ensure the uninterrupted operation of your industrial automation projects, even in the face of supply challenges.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://static.cytron.io/image/tutorial/pi-in-industrial/DIGITAL APPROVED RESELLER LOGO_COLOUR.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>"}];
